// carbon transport model
// XL port of L+C model Mechanistic modelling of coupled phloem/xylem transport for L-systems:
// combining analytical and computational methods
// Original model by Seleznyova and Hanan. (2018)
// Port by Junqi zhu <junqi.zhu@plantandfood.co.nz>
import static globalParameters.*;
import static absOrgan.*;
import static leaf.*;
import static shoot.*;
import static budBase.*;
import static plantBase.*;
import static modelOptions.*;
import static initialConditions.*;
import static plantParameters.*;
import static rootSystem.*;
import static flowerBase.*;
import static fruitBase.*;
import static fineRoot.*;
import static structuralRoot.*;
import static berryComplex.*;
import static virtualFruit.*;
import static diagnosticTables.*;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.TreeMap;

/**
 * Carbon transport model (XL port of the L+C coupled phloem/xylem framework).
 *
 * <p><b>Scope</b> — Implements the Seleznyova & Hanan (2018) analytical + computational
 * approach for mass transport through the phloem, coupled to xylem hydraulics, on top of
 * a GroIMP/XL plant graph. The solver operates in the carbon-potential domain
 * Φ (denoted {@code cp}) with {@code cp = 0.5 * c^2}, where {@code c} is phloem carbon
 * concentration (g C cm⁻³). Nonlinear organ loading/unloading is linearised per Newton step as
 * {@code j(Φ) ≈ a + b · Φ}, with {@code a,b} assembled into per-node branch terms.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Key conventions</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><b>Potential:</b> {@code cp} is carbon potential Φ; {@code cpt}/{@code cpb} are top/bottom
 *       potentials of a transport element.</li>
 *   <li><b>Flux sign:</b> {@code j} is net mass carbon flux (gC·h⁻¹). Positive {@code j} = unloading
 *       from phloem to the organ (sink). Negative {@code j} = loading from organ to phloem (source).</li>
 *   <li><b>Linearisation:</b> Each organ computes {@code sink_source_a} and {@code sink_source_b},
 *       then branch-level accumulators {@code branch_flux_a}, {@code branch_flux_b} are folded
 *       upstream per axis.</li>
 *   <li><b>Resistance/xylem coupling:</b> Transport update uses local phloem resistance {@code r}
 *       and xylem pull term {@code xp}; Munch counter flow is updated from branch flux.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Solver loop</b> (one time step)
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@code linearise(pb, context)} — compute per-organ (a,b).</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateBranchFlux(pb, context)} — fold (a,b) upstream by axis/root to the PlantBase.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonPotential(pb, context)} — UNFOLD potentials from PlantBase to its children.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateFlow(pb, context)} — update organ fluxes j = a + b·cpt and the solve residual.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateResistence(pb)} — refresh phloem resistance and related transport params.</li>
 *   <li>Repeat 1–5 until the existing mixed flux and PlantBase boundary
 *       criteria pass, or the exact iteration limit is reached. Whole-plant
 *       and simple-root closure remain explicit diagnostics.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonStatus(pb)} — compute per-organ sugar, loading/leakage/unloading and Mcf.</li>
 * </ol></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Debugging</b> — Verbose printing is guarded by the global {@code debug_CT} flag; some summaries
 * print unconditionally where noted. The fold/unfold passes use step ticks to warn on double writes.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Units</b> — Fluxes are g C h⁻¹ unless stated. {@code cp} in g² C cm⁻⁶, concentrations in g C cm⁻³
 * (or converted sugar units where noted). Constants are documented inline.</p>
 *
 *******************************************************************************************
 * Revised carbon transport linearisation using sugar-domain source/sink responses.
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose.</b>
 * The carbon transport (CT) solver still operates in the carbon-potential domain,
 * where:
 * <pre>
 *     Phi = cp = 0.5 * c^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * with {@code c} being phloem carbon concentration. The solver requires each
 * organ exchange flux to be locally linearised as:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j(Phi) ~= a + b * Phi
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code j} is the net carbon exchange flux between the organ and the
 * phloem. Positive {@code j} represents unloading from phloem to organ
 * (sink behaviour), while negative {@code j} represents loading from organ
 * to phloem (source behaviour).
 *
 * <p>The revised implementation changes the biological response domain of
 * source loading and sink unloading. Instead of evaluating the loading and
 * unloading response functions directly in {@code Phi}-space, the model now:
 *
 * <ol>
 *   <li>converts local carbon potential {@code Phi} to phloem carbon concentration,</li>
 *   <li>converts phloem carbon concentration to phloem sugar concentration,</li>
 *   <li>evaluates source/sink response functions in sugar concentration space,</li>
 *   <li>uses the chain rule to obtain derivatives with respect to {@code Phi},</li>
 *   <li>builds the standard CT linear coefficients {@code a} and {@code b}.</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <p>This preserves the analytical/iterative CT solver structure while making
 * organ-level source and sink responses more consistent with the CP/common-pool
 * carbon allocation formulation, where limitation functions are naturally
 * parameterised in sugar or concentration space.
 *
 * <h3>Conversion from carbon potential to sugar concentration</h3>
 *
 * <p>The local carbon potential is first converted to carbon concentration:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     c = sqrt(2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * and then converted to phloem sugar concentration through:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     sugar = convertPhloemCtoSugar(c)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This conversion is wrapped by {@code sugarFromCp(cp)}. The derivative used
 * for the chain rule assumes that sugar concentration is proportional to carbon
 * concentration:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dSugar/dPhi = sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * Because this derivative becomes numerically sensitive near {@code Phi = 0},
 * the implementation applies lower bounds to {@code cp} and sugar concentration
 * using {@code CT_CP_MIN} and {@code CT_SUGAR_MIN}.
 *
 * <h3>Sink unloading response in sugar space</h3>
 *
 * <p>Sink unloading is evaluated using a Michaelis-Menten-like response:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     f(sugar; Km) = sugar / (Km + sugar) + epsilon
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code Km} is the sugar-domain half-saturation parameter for the
 * corresponding sink component. Different sink components can use different
 * {@code Km} values, for example:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code km_pri} for primary structural growth demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_sec} for secondary structural growth demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_res} for reserve storage demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code KM_MTNCE} for maintenance demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_res} for fine-root exudation in the current implementation.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>The derivative in sugar space is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     df/dSugar = Km / (Km + sugar)^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * The CT solver needs the derivative with respect to {@code Phi}, therefore:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     df/dPhi = df/dSugar * dSugar/dPhi
 *             = Km / (Km + sugar)^2 * sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This is implemented by {@code dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kmSugar)}.
 *
 * <h3>Source loading response in sugar space</h3>
 *
 * <p>Source loading is evaluated using a logistic response in sugar space:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     g(sugar) = -1 / (1 + exp(b * (sugar - sugar0)))
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code b} is the logistic slope and {@code sugar0} is the sugar-domain
 * inflection point. The negative sign preserves the existing CT convention that
 * source loading into the phloem is a negative exchange flux.
 *
 * <p>The derivative in sugar space is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dg/dSugar = b * exp(b * (sugar - sugar0))
 *                 / (1 + exp(b * (sugar - sugar0)))^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * and the derivative required by the CT solver is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dg/dPhi = dg/dSugar * dSugar/dPhi
 *             = dg/dSugar * sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This is implemented by {@code dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, bSugar, c0Sugar)}.
 * The exponential argument is clamped to avoid overflow.
 *
 * <h3>Organ-level Taylor linearisation</h3>
 *
 * <p>For each organ and each Newton iteration, the current potential
 * {@code Phi0 = o.cpt} is used as the expansion point. For a generic response
 * function {@code h(Phi)}, the first-order Taylor expansion is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     h(Phi) ~= h(Phi0) + h'(Phi0) * (Phi - Phi0)
 * </pre>
 *
 * Multiplying by the corresponding potential flux/demand term {@code PT} gives:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j(Phi) ~= PT * (h0 - Phi0 * hPrime) + PT * hPrime * Phi
 * </pre>
 *
 * Therefore:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     a = PT * (h0 - Phi0 * hPrime)
 *     b = PT * hPrime
 * </pre>
 *
 * <p>For sink components, {@code h} is the sugar-domain unloading response
 * converted back to {@code d/dPhi}. For source loading, {@code h} is the
 * sugar-domain logistic loading response converted back to {@code d/dPhi}.
 *
 * <p>The final organ coefficients are:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     sink_source_a = mgTogram * (sum(sinkA) + loadA)
 *     sink_source_b = mgTogram * (sum(sinkB) + loadB)
 * </pre>
 *
 * and the organ exchange flux used by the CT solver is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j = sink_source_a + sink_source_b * cpt
 * </pre>
 *
 * <h3>Whole-plant CT calculation flow</h3>
 *
 * <p>The revised sugar-domain response functions are used inside the existing
 * CT solve sequence:
 *
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@code linearise(pb, context)} computes local {@code sink_source_a} and
 *       {@code sink_source_b} for each organ.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateBranchFlux(pb, context)} folds local coefficients upstream through
 *       the plant graph to obtain branch-level {@code branch_flux_a} and
 *       {@code branch_flux_b}.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonPotential(pb, context)} solves/unfolds carbon potential from
 *       {@code PlantBase} to downstream transport elements using branch
 *       coefficients, phloem resistance, and xylem-pull terms.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateFlow(pb, context)} recomputes local fluxes as
 *       {@code j = a + b * cpt} and accumulates the convergence residual.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateResistence(pb)} updates concentration-dependent resistance
 *       and transport parameters from the latest local carbon concentration.</li>
 *   <li>The loop repeats until mixed absolute/relative flux and PlantBase
 *       boundary criteria pass, or the exact iteration guard is reached.
 *       Closure and coverage are reported independently.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonStatus(pb)} updates final organ sugar concentration,
 *       carbon allocation state, carbon flux, and Munch counter-flow terms.</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <h3>Parameter interpretation</h3>
 *
 * <p>After this revision, parameters passed to {@code SinkUnloading_fromSugar}
 * and {@code SourceLoading_fromSugar} are interpreted in sugar concentration
 * space, not carbon-potential space. In particular, the legacy parameter name
 * {@code sourceLoading_cp} may be misleading when used as the logistic
 * inflection argument in {@code SourceLoading_fromSugar}; biologically and
 * numerically it should now be interpreted as a sugar-domain threshold.
 *
 * <p>Recommended future cleanup: rename {@code sourceLoading_cp} to a clearer
 * name such as {@code sourceLoadingSugarThreshold} or
 * {@code sourceLoading_sugar_c0}, while preserving backward compatibility in
 * the JSON/config loader if required.
 *
 * <h3>Numerical guards</h3>
 *
 * <p>The revision relies on the following guards:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code CT_CP_MIN}: lower bound for carbon potential before conversion,</li>
 *   <li>{@code CT_SUGAR_MIN}: lower bound for sugar concentration in derivative calculations,</li>
 *   <li>{@code CT_DERIV_MAX}: upper bound for source/sink derivatives with respect to {@code Phi}.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>These guards are required because {@code dSugar/dPhi = sugar / (2 * Phi)}
 * is sensitive near zero carbon potential and can otherwise produce unstable
 * Newton coefficients.
 *
 * @see #SinkUnloading_fromSugar(double, double)
 * @see #dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(double, double)
 * @see #SourceLoading_fromSugar(double, double, double)
 * @see #dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(double, double, double)
 * @see #lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan)
 * @see #linearise(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateBranchFlux(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateFlow(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateResistence(PlantBase)
 * @see #updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase)
 * @author  Port: Junqi Zhu {@code <junqi.zhu@plantandfood.co.nz>}
 * @since   2021 updated on 2025-08
 */


/* #### defines pertinents for the carbon transport model ##################*/
global double INFTY     = 1e10;      // very large number
global double EPSILON   = 1.0/INFTY; // very small number different from zero
// Retained for saved-project compatibility; active solves use mixed CT_* tolerances.
global double MAXERROR  = 1e-5;

global boolean debug_CT = false;

// Retained only so saved GroIMP projects containing the former globals load cleanly.
// Active solves use CarbonTransportSolveContext and never read or write these fields.
global double Serror = 0.0;
global int error_count = 0;

/** Per-call mutable state for one plant's carbon-transport solve. */
class CarbonTransportSolveContext {
  double convergenceError = 0.0;
  double relativeFluxError = 0.0;
  double oldFluxMagnitude = 0.0;
  double newFluxMagnitude = 0.0;
  double fluxScale = 1e-12;
  double fluxNormalizedError = 0.0;
  double plantBaseResidual = 0.0;
  double plantBaseRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  double plantBaseScale = 1e-12;
  double plantBaseNormalizedError = 0.0;
  /** Signed graph-closure residual sum(local j) - folded PlantBase j (g C h-1). */
  double closureResidual = 0.0;
  double closureScale = 1e-12;
  double relativeClosureResidual = 0.0;
  double closureNormalizedError = 0.0;
  double sumLocalJ = 0.0;
  double pbFoldedJ = 0.0;
  double totalLoading = 0.0;
  double totalUnloading = 0.0;
  double netFluxResidual = 0.0;
  double relativeNetFluxResidual = 0.0;
  double netFluxIdentityResidual = 0.0;
  double nonlinearMerit = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  double previousNonlinearMerit = Double.NaN;
  double dampingFactor = 0.5;
  double rawPlantBasePhi = 1e-8;
  double acceptedPlantBasePhi = 1e-8;
  boolean converged = false;
  boolean maxIterationReached = false;
  boolean invalidUnfoldTrial = false;
  int invalidUnfoldTrialCount = 0;
  int totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount = 0;
  boolean retryUsed = false;
  boolean retryConverged = false;
  boolean solverFallbackUsed = false;
  boolean bootstrapFallbackUsed = false;
  int finalIterationLimit = 30;
  int carbonStatusUpdateCount = 0;
  int iterationCount = 0;
  boolean failedTrialCaptured = false;
  double failedTrialPlantBasePhi = 0.0;
  double failedTrialPlantBaseSugar = 0.0;
  double failedTrialMinSugar = 0.0;
  double failedTrialMaxSugar = 0.0;
  double failedTrialMeanSugar = 0.0;
  double failedTrialMerit = 0.0;
  int foldStep = 0;
  int unfoldStep = 0;
  long totalGrowingOrganCount = 0;
  long foldedGrowingOrganCount = 0;
  long unfoldedGrowingOrganCount = 0;
  boolean foldCoverageComplete = false;
  boolean unfoldCoverageComplete = false;
  boolean simpleRootActive = false;
  boolean simpleRootTopologyValid = true;
  boolean simpleRootFoldValid = true;
  boolean simpleRootUnfoldValid = true;
  int simpleRootDoubleFoldCount = 0;
  int simpleRootMinLayer = -1;
  int simpleRootMaxLayer = -1;
  int simpleRootLayerCount = 0;
  long simpleStructuralRootExpected = 0;
  long simpleStructuralRootFolded = 0;
  long simpleStructuralRootUnfolded = 0;
  long simpleFineRootExpected = 0;
  long simpleFineRootFolded = 0;
  long simpleFineRootUnfolded = 0;
  double simpleRootLocalJ = 0.0;
  double simpleRootFoldedJ = 0.0;
  double simpleRootClosureResidual = 0.0;
  double simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual = 0.0;
  double leafA = 0.0, leafB = 0.0, leafJ = 0.0;
  double petioleA = 0.0, petioleB = 0.0, petioleJ = 0.0;
  double shootA = 0.0, shootB = 0.0, shootJ = 0.0;
  double fineRootA = 0.0, fineRootB = 0.0, fineRootJ = 0.0;
  double structuralRootA = 0.0, structuralRootB = 0.0, structuralRootJ = 0.0;
  double fruitA = 0.0, fruitB = 0.0, fruitJ = 0.0;
  double flowerA = 0.0, flowerB = 0.0, flowerJ = 0.0;
  double sumLeafStoredJ = 0.0, sumLeafTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumPetioleStoredJ = 0.0, sumPetioleTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumShootStoredJ = 0.0, sumShootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumFruitStoredJ = 0.0, sumFruitTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumFlowerStoredJ = 0.0, sumFlowerTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumFineRootStoredJ = 0.0, sumFineRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumStructuralRootStoredJ = 0.0, sumStructuralRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  double sumFruitExactUnloading = 0.0;
  double sumFruitExactActive = 0.0;
  double sumFruitExactMassFlow = 0.0;
  double sumFruitStoredUnloading = 0.0;
  double fruitLinearizationResidual = 0.0;
  double fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  double maxFruitLinearizationResidual = 0.0;
  double maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  long maxFruitResidualOrganID = -1L;
  double fruitStoredVsExactResidual = 0.0;
  double maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = 0.0;
  double maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual = 0.0;
}

/**
 * Validated, immutable-within-one-solve carbon-transport connectivity.
 *
 * <p>Graph discovery is performed once at the start of {@code updateC_Transport}.
 * Every nonlinear pass then uses only these raw Java-1.5-compatible collections.
 * This keeps the CT9 ownership and one-transform rules while making the hot path
 * linear in the number of organs and transport edges.</p>
 */
private class CarbonTransportTopology {
  ArrayList growingOrgans = new ArrayList();
  TreeMap internodesById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap petiolesById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap leavesById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap fruitsById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap flowersById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap structuralRootsById = new TreeMap();
  TreeMap fineRootsById = new TreeMap();

  HashMap parentByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap childInternodesByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap childPetiolesByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap childFruitsByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap childFlowersByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap directLeavesByInternode = new HashMap();
  HashMap leavesByPetiole = new HashMap();
  HashMap leafTransportOwner = new HashMap();
  HashMap petioleOwnerByLeaf = new HashMap();

  ArrayList shootPostOrder = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList shootPreOrder = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList basalShootIds = new ArrayList();

  ArrayList structuralRoots = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList fineRoots = new ArrayList();
  HashMap fineRootOwnerById = new HashMap();
  HashMap structuralRootByLayer = new HashMap();
  HashMap fineRootByLayer = new HashMap();
  ArrayList simpleStructuralRoots = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList simpleFineRoots = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList simpleRootFoldOrder = new ArrayList();
  ArrayList simpleRootUnfoldOrder = new ArrayList();
  StructuralRoot simpleBasalRoot = null;

  int simpleRootMinLayer = -1;
  int simpleRootMaxLayer = -1;
  int maxLastFoldStep = -1;
  int maxLastUnfoldStep = -1;
  int ambiguousLeafOwners = 0;
  int missingLeafOwners = 0;
  int ambiguousFineRootOwners = 0;
  int missingFineRootOwners = 0;
  boolean valid = true;
  String error = "";

  void invalidate(String message) {
    if (valid) error = message;
    valid = false;
  }

  void registerPetioleLeaf(Petiole petioleNode, Leaf leafNode) {
    if (petioleNode == null || leafNode == null) return;
    Long petioleKey = Long.valueOf(petioleNode.getId());
    Long leafKey = Long.valueOf(leafNode.getId());
    if (!petiolesById.containsKey(petioleKey)
        || !leavesById.containsKey(leafKey)) {
      invalidate("Petiole-Leaf relation contains an organ outside the collected plant");
      return;
    }
    Long previousOwner = (Long) petioleOwnerByLeaf.get(leafKey);
    if (previousOwner == null) {
      petioleOwnerByLeaf.put(leafKey, petioleKey);
    } else if (previousOwner.longValue() != petioleKey.longValue()) {
      ambiguousLeafOwners++;
      invalidate("ambiguous Petiole owners for leafId=" + leafKey
          + " ownerIds=" + previousOwner + "," + petioleKey);
    }
  }
}

private static ArrayList ctList(HashMap map, Long key) {
  ArrayList values = (ArrayList) map.get(key);
  if (values == null) {
    values = new ArrayList();
    map.put(key, values);
  }
  return values;
}

/** Generate deterministic child-before-parent and parent-before-child orders. */
private static boolean generateCarbonShootTraversalOrders(
    CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  HashMap remainingChildren = new HashMap();
  ArrayList queue = new ArrayList();
  for (Object keyObject : topology.internodesById.keySet()) {
    Long key = (Long) keyObject;
    ArrayList children = ctList(topology.childInternodesByInternode, key);
    java.util.Collections.sort(children);
    remainingChildren.put(key, Integer.valueOf(children.size()));
    if (children.size() == 0) queue.add(key);
  }

  int queueIndex = 0;
  while (queueIndex < queue.size()) {
    Long childId = (Long) queue.get(queueIndex++);
    topology.shootPostOrder.add(childId);
    Long parentId = (Long) topology.parentByInternode.get(childId);
    if (parentId != null) {
      Integer remaining = (Integer) remainingChildren.get(parentId);
      if (remaining == null) {
        topology.invalidate("missing shoot traversal state for parentId=" + parentId);
        return false;
      }
      int next = remaining.intValue() - 1;
      remainingChildren.put(parentId, Integer.valueOf(next));
      if (next == 0) queue.add(parentId);
    }
  }
  if (topology.shootPostOrder.size() != topology.internodesById.size()) {
    topology.invalidate("cycle or unresolved shoot topology: postOrder="
        + topology.shootPostOrder.size() + " internodes="
        + topology.internodesById.size());
    return false;
  }

  java.util.Collections.sort(topology.basalShootIds);
  queue.clear();
  queue.addAll(topology.basalShootIds);
  queueIndex = 0;
  HashSet visited = new HashSet();
  while (queueIndex < queue.size()) {
    Long parentId = (Long) queue.get(queueIndex++);
    if (!visited.add(parentId)) {
      topology.invalidate("duplicate shoot preorder visit at internodeId=" + parentId);
      return false;
    }
    topology.shootPreOrder.add(parentId);
    queue.addAll(ctList(topology.childInternodesByInternode, parentId));
  }
  if (topology.shootPreOrder.size() != topology.internodesById.size()) {
    topology.invalidate("disconnected shoot topology: preOrder="
        + topology.shootPreOrder.size() + " internodes="
        + topology.internodesById.size());
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}

private static void registerCarbonFineRootOwner(
    CarbonTransportTopology topology, FineRoot fineRootNode,
    StructuralRoot rootOwner) {
  if (topology == null || fineRootNode == null || rootOwner == null) return;
  Long fineKey = Long.valueOf(fineRootNode.getId());
  Long ownerKey = Long.valueOf(rootOwner.getId());
  Long previousOwner = (Long) topology.fineRootOwnerById.get(fineKey);
  if (previousOwner == null) {
    topology.fineRootOwnerById.put(fineKey, ownerKey);
  } else if (previousOwner.longValue() != ownerKey.longValue()) {
    topology.ambiguousFineRootOwners++;
  }
}

/** Validate the existing one-StructuralRoot/one-FineRoot-per-layer route once. */
private static void validateSimpleCarbonRootTopology(
    PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  if (topology.ambiguousFineRootOwners > 0
      || topology.missingFineRootOwners > 0) {
    topology.invalidate("invalid simple-root transport ownership: ambiguous="
        + topology.ambiguousFineRootOwners + " missing="
        + topology.missingFineRootOwners);
  }
  int structuralCount = topology.structuralRoots.size();
  int fineCount = topology.fineRoots.size();
  if (structuralCount <= 0) {
    topology.invalidate("simple-root topology contains no StructuralRoot");
    return;
  }

  for (int rootIndex = 0; rootIndex < structuralCount; rootIndex++) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot) topology.structuralRoots.get(rootIndex);
    Integer layerKey = Integer.valueOf(rootNode.layer);
    if (topology.structuralRootByLayer.put(layerKey, rootNode) != null) {
      topology.invalidate("multiple StructuralRoot nodes at simple-root layer="
          + rootNode.layer);
    }
    if (topology.simpleRootMinLayer < 0
        || rootNode.layer < topology.simpleRootMinLayer) {
      topology.simpleRootMinLayer = rootNode.layer;
    }
    if (topology.simpleRootMaxLayer < 0
        || rootNode.layer > topology.simpleRootMaxLayer) {
      topology.simpleRootMaxLayer = rootNode.layer;
    }
  }
  for (int fineIndex = 0; fineIndex < fineCount; fineIndex++) {
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.fineRoots.get(fineIndex);
    Integer layerKey = Integer.valueOf(fineNode.layer);
    if (topology.fineRootByLayer.put(layerKey, fineNode) != null) {
      topology.invalidate("multiple FineRoot nodes at simple-root layer="
          + fineNode.layer);
    }
  }

  int layerCount = topology.simpleRootMaxLayer
      - topology.simpleRootMinLayer + 1;
  if (topology.simpleRootMinLayer != 0
      || structuralCount != layerCount
      || fineCount != layerCount
      || layerCount != numofSoilLayers) {
    topology.invalidate("invalid simple-root layer coverage: min="
        + topology.simpleRootMinLayer + " max=" + topology.simpleRootMaxLayer
        + " structuralRoots=" + structuralCount + " fineRoots=" + fineCount
        + " configuredLayers=" + numofSoilLayers);
  }

  StructuralRoot previousRoot = null;
  int layer;
  for (layer = topology.simpleRootMinLayer;
      layer <= topology.simpleRootMaxLayer; layer++) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.structuralRootByLayer.get(Integer.valueOf(layer));
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot)
        topology.fineRootByLayer.get(Integer.valueOf(layer));
    boolean layerValid = rootNode != null && fineNode != null;
    if (layerValid) {
      layerValid = fineNode.parentID == rootNode.getId()
          && rootNode.frID == fineNode.getId()
          && fineNode.plantNumber == rootNode.plantNumber
          && fineNode.layer == rootNode.layer;
    }
    if (layerValid && previousRoot == null) {
      layerValid = pb.childStructuralRootID == rootNode.getId()
          && rootNode.parentID == pb.getId();
      topology.simpleBasalRoot = rootNode;
    } else if (layerValid) {
      layerValid = rootNode.parentID == previousRoot.getId()
          && ctStructuralRootHasChildId(previousRoot, rootNode.getId());
    }
    if (!layerValid) {
      topology.invalidate("invalid simple-root ownership at layer=" + layer);
    }
    if (rootNode != null) {
      topology.simpleStructuralRoots.add(rootNode);
      topology.simpleRootUnfoldOrder.add(rootNode);
      previousRoot = rootNode;
    }
    if (fineNode != null) topology.simpleFineRoots.add(fineNode);
  }
  for (int rootIndex = topology.simpleStructuralRoots.size() - 1;
      rootIndex >= 0; rootIndex--) {
    topology.simpleRootFoldOrder.add(
        topology.simpleStructuralRoots.get(rootIndex));
  }
}

/** Resolve Petiole--Leaf topology exactly once per hourly solve. */
private static void collectCarbonPetioleLeafRelations(
    PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportTopology topology) [
  petioleOwner:Petiole (-->){1,5} ownedLeaf:Leaf, (
    petioleOwner.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    && ownedLeaf.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    topology.registerPetioleLeaf(petioleOwner, ownedLeaf);
  }
]

private static CarbonTransportTopology buildCarbonTransportTopology(
    PlantBase pb, GrowingOrgan[] collectedOrgans) {
  CarbonTransportTopology topology = new CarbonTransportTopology();
  TreeMap allById = new TreeMap();
  int organIndex;
  for (organIndex = 0; organIndex < collectedOrgans.length; organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = collectedOrgans[organIndex];
    if (organ == null) {
      topology.invalidate("null GrowingOrgan at collected index=" + organIndex);
      continue;
    }
    if (organ.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) {
      topology.invalidate("GrowingOrgan from another plant at id=" + organ.getId());
      continue;
    }
    long organId = organ.getId();
    Long organKey = Long.valueOf(organId);
    if (organId <= 0L || allById.put(organKey, organ) != null) {
      topology.invalidate("duplicate or invalid GrowingOrgan id=" + organId);
      continue;
    }
    topology.maxLastFoldStep = Math.max(
        topology.maxLastFoldStep, organ.lastFoldStep);
    topology.maxLastUnfoldStep = Math.max(
        topology.maxLastUnfoldStep, organ.lastUnfoldStep);
    if (organ instanceof Internode) topology.internodesById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof Petiole) topology.petiolesById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof Leaf) topology.leavesById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof FruitService) topology.fruitsById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof Flower) topology.flowersById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof StructuralRoot) topology.structuralRootsById.put(organKey, organ);
    else if (organ instanceof FineRoot) topology.fineRootsById.put(organKey, organ);
    else topology.invalidate("unsupported GrowingOrgan class="
        + organ.getClass().getSimpleName() + " id=" + organId);
  }
  topology.growingOrgans.addAll(allById.values());
  topology.structuralRoots.addAll(topology.structuralRootsById.values());
  topology.fineRoots.addAll(topology.fineRootsById.values());

  for (Object keyObject : topology.internodesById.keySet()) {
    Long key = (Long) keyObject;
    topology.childInternodesByInternode.put(key, new ArrayList());
    topology.childPetiolesByInternode.put(key, new ArrayList());
    topology.childFruitsByInternode.put(key, new ArrayList());
    topology.childFlowersByInternode.put(key, new ArrayList());
    topology.directLeavesByInternode.put(key, new ArrayList());
  }
  for (Object keyObject : topology.petiolesById.keySet()) {
    topology.leavesByPetiole.put((Long) keyObject, new ArrayList());
  }

  for (Object keyObject : topology.internodesById.keySet()) {
    Long childKey = (Long) keyObject;
    Internode child = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(childKey);
    Long parentKey = Long.valueOf(child.parentID);
    if (topology.internodesById.containsKey(parentKey)) {
      if (parentKey.longValue() == childKey.longValue()) {
        topology.invalidate("self-parent internodeId=" + childKey);
      } else {
        topology.parentByInternode.put(childKey, parentKey);
        ctList(topology.childInternodesByInternode, parentKey).add(childKey);
      }
    } else if (child.parentID <= 0L || child.parentID == pb.getId()) {
      topology.basalShootIds.add(childKey);
    } else {
      topology.invalidate("missing Internode parent: childId=" + childKey
          + " parentId=" + child.parentID);
    }
  }

  for (Object keyObject : topology.petiolesById.keySet()) {
    Long childKey = (Long) keyObject;
    Petiole child = (Petiole) topology.petiolesById.get(childKey);
    Long parentKey = Long.valueOf(child.parentID);
    if (topology.internodesById.containsKey(parentKey)) {
      ctList(topology.childPetiolesByInternode, parentKey).add(child);
    } else {
      topology.invalidate("missing Internode owner for Petiole id=" + childKey
          + " parentId=" + child.parentID);
    }
  }
  for (Object keyObject : topology.fruitsById.keySet()) {
    Long childKey = (Long) keyObject;
    FruitService child = (FruitService) topology.fruitsById.get(childKey);
    Long parentKey = Long.valueOf(child.parentID);
    if (topology.internodesById.containsKey(parentKey)) {
      ctList(topology.childFruitsByInternode, parentKey).add(child);
    } else {
      topology.invalidate("missing Internode owner for Fruit id=" + childKey
          + " parentId=" + child.parentID);
    }
  }
  for (Object keyObject : topology.flowersById.keySet()) {
    Long childKey = (Long) keyObject;
    Flower child = (Flower) topology.flowersById.get(childKey);
    Long parentKey = Long.valueOf(child.parentID);
    if (topology.internodesById.containsKey(parentKey)) {
      ctList(topology.childFlowersByInternode, parentKey).add(child);
    } else {
      topology.invalidate("missing Internode owner for Flower id=" + childKey
          + " parentId=" + child.parentID);
    }
  }

  for (Object fineKeyObject : topology.fineRootsById.keySet()) {
    Long fineKey = (Long) fineKeyObject;
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.fineRootsById.get(fineKey);
    StructuralRoot pointerParent = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.structuralRootsById.get(Long.valueOf(fineNode.parentID));
    registerCarbonFineRootOwner(topology, fineNode, pointerParent);
  }
  for (Object rootKeyObject : topology.structuralRootsById.keySet()) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.structuralRootsById.get((Long) rootKeyObject);
    FineRoot linkedFine = (FineRoot)
        topology.fineRootsById.get(Long.valueOf(rootNode.frID));
    registerCarbonFineRootOwner(topology, linkedFine, rootNode);
  }
  for (Object fineKeyObject : topology.fineRootsById.keySet()) {
    Long fineKey = (Long) fineKeyObject;
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.fineRootsById.get(fineKey);
    Long ownerKey = (Long) topology.fineRootOwnerById.get(fineKey);
    fineNode.ctTransportOwnerId = (ownerKey == null)
        ? -1L : ownerKey.longValue();
    fineNode.ctTransportOwnerCount = (ownerKey == null) ? 0 : 1;
    if (ownerKey == null) topology.missingFineRootOwners++;
  }

  collectCarbonPetioleLeafRelations(pb, topology);
  for (Object leafKeyObject : topology.leavesById.keySet()) {
    Long leafKey = (Long) leafKeyObject;
    Leaf leafNode = (Leaf) topology.leavesById.get(leafKey);
    Long petioleKey = (Long) topology.petioleOwnerByLeaf.get(leafKey);
    if (petioleKey != null) {
      Petiole owner = (Petiole) topology.petiolesById.get(petioleKey);
      topology.leafTransportOwner.put(leafKey, owner);
      ctList(topology.leavesByPetiole, petioleKey).add(leafNode);
      leafNode.ctTransportOwnerId = petioleKey.longValue();
      leafNode.ctTransportOwnerCount = 1;
    } else {
      Long parentKey = Long.valueOf(leafNode.parentID);
      Internode owner = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(parentKey);
      if (owner == null) {
        topology.missingLeafOwners++;
        topology.invalidate("missing CT owner for Leaf id=" + leafKey
            + " parentId=" + leafNode.parentID);
        leafNode.ctTransportOwnerId = -1L;
        leafNode.ctTransportOwnerCount = 0;
      } else {
        topology.leafTransportOwner.put(leafKey, owner);
        ctList(topology.directLeavesByInternode, parentKey).add(leafNode);
        leafNode.ctTransportOwnerId = -1L;
        leafNode.ctTransportOwnerCount = 0;
      }
    }
  }

  if (topology.internodesById.size() > 0
      && topology.basalShootIds.size() == 0) {
    topology.invalidate("no basal Internode for PlantBase id=" + pb.getId());
  }
  if (topology.valid) generateCarbonShootTraversalOrders(topology);
  if (useComplexRoot == false) validateSimpleCarbonRootTopology(pb, topology);
  return topology;
}

/** Accepted transport/rate state for one organ before the hourly CT solve. */
class CarbonTransportOrganState {
  GrowingOrgan organ;
  double cpb, cpt, j, r, xp;
  double sinkSourceA, sinkSourceB, branchFluxA, branchFluxB, err;
  double structurePriPt, structureSecPt, maintenancePt, reservePt, loadingPt;
  double structure, structurePri, structureSec, maintenance, reserve;
  float loading, leakage;
  double unloading, carbonFlux, munchCounterFlow, biomassSupply, biomassDemand;

  CarbonTransportOrganState(GrowingOrgan target) {
    organ = target;
    cpb = target.cpb; cpt = target.cpt; j = target.j;
    r = target.r; xp = target.xp;
    sinkSourceA = target.sink_source_a;
    sinkSourceB = target.sink_source_b;
    branchFluxA = target.branch_flux_a;
    branchFluxB = target.branch_flux_b;
    err = target.err;
    structurePriPt = target.structureDM_PRI_PT;
    structureSecPt = target.structureDM_SEC_PT;
    maintenancePt = target.maintenanceDM_PT;
    reservePt = target.reserveDM_PT;
    loadingPt = target.loading_PT;
    structure = target.structureDM;
    structurePri = target.structureDM_PRI;
    structureSec = target.structureDM_SEC;
    maintenance = target.maintenanceDM;
    reserve = target.reserveDM;
    loading = target.loading;
    leakage = target.leakage;
    unloading = target.unloading;
    carbonFlux = target.Cflux;
    munchCounterFlow = target.Mcf;
    biomassSupply = target.biomassSupply;
    biomassDemand = target.biomassDemand;
  }

  void restore() {
    if (organ == null) return;
    organ.cpb = cpb; organ.cpt = cpt; organ.j = j;
    organ.r = r; organ.xp = xp;
    organ.sink_source_a = sinkSourceA;
    organ.sink_source_b = sinkSourceB;
    organ.branch_flux_a = branchFluxA;
    organ.branch_flux_b = branchFluxB;
    organ.err = err;
    organ.structureDM_PRI_PT = structurePriPt;
    organ.structureDM_SEC_PT = structureSecPt;
    organ.maintenanceDM_PT = maintenancePt;
    organ.reserveDM_PT = reservePt;
    organ.loading_PT = loadingPt;
    organ.structureDM = structure;
    organ.structureDM_PRI = structurePri;
    organ.structureDM_SEC = structureSec;
    organ.maintenanceDM = maintenance;
    organ.reserveDM = reserve;
    organ.loading = loading;
    organ.leakage = leakage;
    organ.unloading = unloading;
    organ.Cflux = carbonFlux;
    organ.Mcf = munchCounterFlow;
    organ.biomassSupply = biomassSupply;
    organ.biomassDemand = biomassDemand;
  }
}

/** Accepted PlantBase and organ transport state used by retry and fallback. */
class CarbonTransportStateSnapshot {
  PlantBase plantBase;
  java.util.ArrayList organStates = new java.util.ArrayList();
  double cpb, cpt, j, r, xp;
  double branchFluxA, branchFluxB;
  double sugar, previousSugar;

  CarbonTransportStateSnapshot(PlantBase target) {
    plantBase = target;
    cpb = target.cpb; cpt = target.cpt; j = target.j;
    r = target.r; xp = target.xp;
    branchFluxA = target.branch_flux_a;
    branchFluxB = target.branch_flux_b;
    sugar = target.sugarConcentration_phloem;
    previousSugar = target.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre;
  }

  void restorePlantBase() {
    if (plantBase == null) return;
    plantBase.cpb = cpb; plantBase.cpt = cpt; plantBase.j = j;
    plantBase.r = r; plantBase.xp = xp;
    plantBase.branch_flux_a = branchFluxA;
    plantBase.branch_flux_b = branchFluxB;
    plantBase.sugarConcentration_phloem = sugar;
    plantBase.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre = previousSugar;
  }
}

// CT response is evaluated in sugar concentration domain and linearised d/dPhi.
static final double CT_CP_MIN = 1e-10;
static final double CT_SUGAR_MIN = 1e-9;
static final double CT_DERIV_MAX = 1e9;
static final double CT_PHI_FLOOR = 1e-8;
// g C h-1 per unit Phi; guards only numerically degenerate folded boundaries.
static final double CT_PB_B_ABS_MIN = 1e-12;
// Numerical solver controls; these do not alter biological source/sink functions.
static final double CT_ABS_FLUX_TOL = 1e-5; // g C h-1
static final double CT_REL_FLUX_TOL = 1e-4; // dimensionless
// A fixed fruit mass-flow boundary restores the original full Newton trial.
static final double CT_DAMPING_INITIAL = 1.0;
static final double CT_DAMPING_MIN = 0.05;
static final double CT_DAMPING_MAX = 1.0;
static final int CT_MAX_ITERATIONS = 30;
static final double CT_RETRY_DAMPING_INITIAL = 0.1;
static final int CT_RETRY_MAX_ITERATIONS = 60;

// defines pertinent to test case 
// constant source and sink
global double SOURCEj = 0; //-0.4;  	    // [g h-1] maximum initial influx from the source (for initialization of the system)  
//global double SINKj = 0.5;            // [g h-1] maximun possible influx into the terminal sink
 
global double SOURCEcp = 0.0002;   //calculate carbon potential for sourceLoading_cp; initial value is important; far from the answer can cause nan value
global double initial_c0 = Math.sqrt(2*SOURCEcp);
// defines pertinent to phloem resistance
global double R0 = 0.847E-3;	  // [MPa cm-4 h] //resistance at zero phloem sugar concentration
global double R_ct = 0.024298245614035;  // [MPa cm3 g-1 K-1] //universal gas constant
//global double Tk = 293.15;             // [K]

// defines pertinent to water potential
//global double Rx = 1.0063894024855E-6;          // [cm-4 h] resistance per unit length of xylem
global double MolalVolumeSucrose = 0.6301;      // [g-1 cm3]  



/* #### defines the functions for the carbon transport model ##################*/

/**
 * CP-style unloading response evaluated in sugar concentration space, then used by
 * the CT Phi-domain solver through Taylor linearisation in {@link #lineariseOrgan}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param kmSugar half-saturation sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return unloading activity in sugar domain (unitless multiplier before PT scaling)
 */
static double SinkUnloading_fromSugar(double cp, double kmSugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        sugar = 0.0;
    }
    double km = kmSugar;
    if (Double.isNaN(km) || km <= 0.0) {
        km = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    return sugar / (km + sugar) + 1e-6;
}

/**
 * Chain-rule derivative dS/dPhi for {@link #SinkUnloading_fromSugar}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param kmSugar half-saturation sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return dS/dPhi with numerical guards near Phi=0
 */
static double dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(double cp, double kmSugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < CT_SUGAR_MIN) {
        sugar = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double km = kmSugar;
    if (Double.isNaN(km) || km <= 0.0) {
        km = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double dS_dSugar = km / ((km + sugar) * (km + sugar));
    double dSugar_dCp = sugar / (2.0 * cpEff);
    double out = dS_dSugar * dSugar_dCp;
    if (Double.isNaN(out) || out < 0.0) {
        out = 0.0;
    }
    if (out > CT_DERIV_MAX) {
        out = CT_DERIV_MAX;
    }
    return out + 1e-20;
}


/**
 * CP-style source loading response evaluated in the sugar concentration domain.
 * Negative return value preserves the existing source-loading sign convention.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param bSugar logistic slope in sugar concentration space
 * @param c0Sugar logistic inflection sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return loading activity (negative, before PT scaling)
 */
static double SourceLoading_fromSugar(double cp, double bSugar, double c0Sugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        sugar = 0.0;
    }
    double expArg = bSugar * (sugar - c0Sugar);
    if (expArg > 100.0) expArg = 100.0;
    if (expArg < -100.0) expArg = -100.0;
    double e = Math.exp(expArg);
    return -1.0 / (1.0 + e);
}

/**
 * Chain-rule derivative dLoading/dPhi for {@link #SourceLoading_fromSugar}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param bSugar logistic slope in sugar concentration space
 * @param c0Sugar logistic inflection sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return dLoading/dPhi, clamped for numerical stability
 */
static double dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(double cp, double bSugar, double c0Sugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < CT_SUGAR_MIN) {
        sugar = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double expArg = bSugar * (sugar - c0Sugar);
    if (expArg > 700.0) expArg = 700.0;
    if (expArg < -700.0) expArg = -700.0;
    double e = Math.exp(expArg);
    double dg_dSugar = bSugar * e / ((1.0 + e) * (1.0 + e));
    double dSugar_dCp = sugar / (2.0 * cpEff);
    double out = dg_dSugar * dSugar_dCp;
    if (Double.isNaN(out)) {
        out = 0.0;
    }
    if (Math.abs(out) > CT_DERIV_MAX) {
        out = Math.signum(out) * CT_DERIV_MAX;
    }
    return out;
}

/////////ALTERNATIVE FUNCTION IF YOU WANT TO DO DERIVATIVE REGARDING TO C//////////

// phloem resistance ratio R_ct/R0
/**
 * Empirical phloem resistance ratio as a function of phloem carbon concentration.
 *
 * @param cab phloem carbon concentration (g C cm⁻³)
 * @return R_ct/R0 ratio (dimensionless)
 */
static double PhloemResistanceRatio_sucrose (double cab) 
{
  double  k1 = 0.19961;
  double  k2 = 1.00954;
  double  k3 = -2.2249;
  double  k4 = 1.2776; 
  return (1.0+k1*cab+k2*cab*cab)/(1.0+k3*cab+k4*cab*cab);			 
} 

//Osmotic pressure ratio P/RT
/**
 * Osmotic pressure ratio P/(R·T) as a function of phloem carbon concentration.
 *
 * @param cab phloem carbon concentration (g C cm⁻³)
 * @return P/(R·T) (dimensionless)
 @FIXME fix the effects of sorbital form on pressure ratio. 
 * double cabEq = cabTotal_gC_cm3 * ((1.0 - fSor)*1.0 + fSor*MOL_EQ_FACTOR);
 * double P_over_RT = PressureRatio(cabEq);

 */
static double PressureRatio (double cab) 
{
  double  a = 1.03913;
  double  b = 0.86536;
  double  c = 5.2465;
  //quick scalling for the osmotic potential ratio to RT
  double cabEq = cab * ((1.0 - FRACTION_SORBITOL)*1.0 + FRACTION_SORBITOL* (MOL_SURCROSE/MOL_SORBITOL));
  return (a + b*cabEq + c*cabEq*cabEq);			 
}
// ---- constants you already have (names are examples) ----
static final double CF_SUC = CARBON_FRACTION_SUCROSE;   // ~0.42 gC/g sucrose
static final double CF_SOR = CARBON_FRACTION_SORBITOL;  // ~0.40 gC/g sorbitol
static final double RHO_WATER_25C = 1.0;               // g/cm3, good 5–25% w/w


// Minimal η/ηwater fits at 25 °C vs weight fraction w (0–0.3). Replace when you fit CRC points.
static double etaRelSucrose(double w){ return 1.0 + 2.4*w + 12.0*w*w; }
static double etaRelSorbitol(double w){ return 1.0 + 1.6*w + 6.5*w*w; }

// helpers
static double soluteMassPerCm3(double cab, double carbonFrac){ return cab / Math.max(1e-12, carbonFrac); }
static double weightFraction(double gs){ return gs / (gs + RHO_WATER_25C); } // gs = g solute per cm3

// FRACTION_SORBITOL in [0,1]
static double PhloemResistanceRatio_mixture(double cab, double FRACTION_SORBITOL){
    // split carbon between species
    double cabSor = cab * FRACTION_SORBITOL;
    double cabSuc = cab * (1.0 - FRACTION_SORBITOL);

    // convert to g solute / cm3 (approx density)
    double gsSor = soluteMassPerCm3(cabSor, CF_SOR);
    double gsSuc = soluteMassPerCm3(cabSuc, CF_SUC);
    double gsTot = gsSor + gsSuc;
    double wTot  = weightFraction(gsTot);     // overall wt% as fraction 0–1

    // log-additivity for viscosity of two non-electrolytes (Grunberg–Nissan with G12≈0)
    double xSuc = (gsTot > 0) ? gsSuc / gsTot : 0.0;
    double xSor = 1.0 - xSuc;
    double etaRelMix = Math.exp(xSuc*Math.log(etaRelSucrose(wTot)) + xSor*Math.log(etaRelSorbitol(wTot)));

    // reference (what your k1..k4 implicitly used)
    double etaRelRef = etaRelSucrose(wTot);

    // scale sucrose baseline by viscosity ratio
    return PhloemResistanceRatio_sucrose(cab) * (etaRelMix / Math.max(1e-12, etaRelRef));
}

/** cp → phloem sugar concentration (g sugar cm⁻³). 
 * Convert carbon potential to sugar concentration (model’s sugar unit).
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Φ (≥0)
 * @return sugar concentration (g sugar cm⁻³)
 */
static double sugarFromCp(double cp) {
  double c = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.0, 2.0 * cp));     // c = √(2cp), guard cp≥0
  return convertPhloemCtoSugar((double) c);
}

/** Fail before CSV emission when selected PlantBase sugar and Phi disagree. */
static void verifyPlantBaseSugarForOutput(PlantBase pb,
        double outputSugar) {
  if (pb == null) {
    throw new IllegalStateException(
        "CT plant-level output requires a selected PlantBase.");
  }
  if (!isValidPhi(pb.cpt)) {
    throw new IllegalStateException("CT plant-level output has invalid PlantBase Phi"
        + " pbId=" + pb.getId() + " plantNumber=" + pb.plantNumber
        + " cpt=" + pb.cpt);
  }
  double transformedSugar = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
  double comparisonScale = Math.max(1.0, Math.max(
      Math.abs(transformedSugar), Math.max(
          Math.abs(pb.sugarConcentration_phloem), Math.abs(outputSugar))));
  double comparisonTolerance = 1e-12 * comparisonScale;
  if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(transformedSugar)
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(pb.sugarConcentration_phloem)
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(outputSugar)
      || Math.abs(pb.sugarConcentration_phloem - transformedSugar)
          > comparisonTolerance
      || Math.abs(outputSugar - transformedSugar) > comparisonTolerance) {
    throw new IllegalStateException("CT PlantBase/output sugar mismatch"
        + " pbId=" + pb.getId() + " plantNumber=" + pb.plantNumber
        + " storedSugar=" + pb.sugarConcentration_phloem
        + " sugarFromCpt=" + transformedSugar
        + " outputSugar=" + outputSugar);
  }
}
/** KM in sugar domain → KM in cp domain: cp = 0.5 * c² (with c in gC cm⁻³). 
 * Convert Michaelis constant from sugar-concentration space to potential space.
 *
 * @param km_sugar KM in sugar domain (g sugar cm⁻³)
 * @return KM in cp domain (g² C cm⁻⁶)
 */
static double kmSugarToCp(double km_sugar) {
  double c = convertSugarToPhloemC((double) km_sugar); // sugar → phloem C
  return 0.5 * c * c;
}



/**
 * Linearise sinks and sources for a single organ (fills sink_source_a/b).
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose</b> — Compute the first-order (Taylor) linearisation of the organ’s
 * net phloem exchange <code>j(Φ)</code> around the current carbon potential
 * <code>Φ = cp = o.cpt</code>, so the solver can use
 * <code>j ≈ a + b · Φ</code> within a Newton step.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Inputs used</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><code>o.cpt</code> (top-side carbon potential Φ) and <code>o.cpb</code> (bottom-side guard).</li>
 *   <li>Organ PT multipliers: <code>o.loading_PT</code>, <code>o.structureDM_PRI_PT</code>,
 *       <code>o.structureDM_SEC_PT</code>, <code>o.reserveDM_PT</code>, <code>o.maintenanceDM_PT</code>.</li>
 *   <li>Km-like parameters (in sugar domain) converted to Φ-domain via
 *       <code>cp = 0.5 · c²</code>: <code>o.km_pri</code>, <code>o.km_sec</code>, <code>o.km_res</code>,
 *       and <code>KM_MTNCE</code>.</li>
 *   <li>Model kernels in Φ-domain: <code>SourceLoading(Φ,…)</code>,
 *       <code>dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ,…)</code>, <code>SinkUnloading(Φ,q)</code>,
 *       <code>dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ,q)</code>.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Outputs / side effects</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Sets <code>o.sink_source_a</code> and <code>o.sink_source_b</code> (same mass-flow units as <code>j</code>;
 *       <code>b</code> is “per-Φ” slope). Positive values contribute to unloading (sink), negative to loading (source).</li>
 *   <li>Clamps invalid potentials and applies small-Φ safeguards for derivative stability.</li>
 *   <li>Optionally prints a per-organ debug_CT line when <code>debug_CT</code> is true for selected organ classes.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Definition of the linear terms</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><b>a (intercept)</b>:
 *     <code>a = j(Φ₀) − Φ₀ · j′(Φ₀)</code>, evaluated at <code>Φ₀ = o.cpt</code>.
 *     In code this is the sum over unloading components
 *     <code>PT · (SinkUnloading(Φ₀,q) − Φ₀ · dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ₀,q))</code>
 *     plus the analogous loading term
 *     <code>o.loading_PT · (SourceLoading(Φ₀,…) − Φ₀ · dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ₀,…))</code>.
 *   </li>
 *   <li><b>b (slope)</b>:
 *     <code>b = j′(Φ₀)</code>, the derivative w.r.t. Φ at <code>Φ₀</code>.
 *     In code this is the sum over unloading components
 *     <code>PT · dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ₀,q)</code> plus the loading derivative
 *     <code>o.loading_PT · dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ₀,…)</code>.
 *   </li>
 * </ul>
 * This yields the local linear form <code>j(Φ) ≈ a + b · Φ</code> that the transport solver
 * uses to assemble branch fluxes and update potentials.</p>
 */
static void lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan o) {
  if (o == null) return;

  // Basic guards
  if (Double.isNaN(o.cpb) || o.cpb < 0.0) o.cpb = 1e-5;
  if (Double.isNaN(o.cpt) || o.cpt < 0.0) o.cpt = 1e-5;
  // Current state (Φ-domain uses cp = c^2/2)
  double cp = o.cpt;                           // carbon potential Φ at organ
  double sugar = sugarFromCp(cp);              // current sugar (used by organ to update PT)
  
  
  o.updateCarbonAllocation(sugar);
  // --- Source (loading) linearisation: sugar-domain response, a + b * cp.
  double loadA = 0.0, loadB = 0.0;
  if (o.loading_PT > 0.0) {
    double cp_eff = (cp > CT_CP_MIN) ? cp : CT_CP_MIN;
    double g0 = SourceLoading_fromSugar(cp_eff, sourceLoading_b, sourceLoading_cp);
    double dg = dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(cp_eff, sourceLoading_b, sourceLoading_cp);
    loadA = o.loading_PT * (g0 - cp_eff * dg);
    loadB = o.loading_PT * dg;
  }

  double kPRI = o.km_pri;
  double kSEC = o.km_sec;
  double kRES = o.km_res;
  double kMNT = KM_MTNCE;
  double fPRI = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kPRI);
  double fSEC = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kSEC);
  double fRES = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kRES);
  double fMNT = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kMNT);
  double dPRI = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kPRI);
  double dSEC = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kSEC);
  double dRES = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kRES);
  double dMNT = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kMNT);
  if (o.shouldUsePreT1PotentialGrowth()) {
    // Primary potential growth is intentionally carbon-unlimited before T1.
    fPRI = 1.0;
    dPRI = 0.0;
  }
  double sA_pri = o.structureDM_PRI_PT * (fPRI - cp * dPRI);
  double sA_sec = o.structureDM_SEC_PT * (fSEC - cp * dSEC);
  double sA_res = o.reserveDM_PT       * (fRES - cp * dRES);
  double sA_mnt = o.maintenanceDM_PT   * (fMNT - cp * dMNT);
  double sB_pri = o.structureDM_PRI_PT * dPRI;
  double sB_sec = o.structureDM_SEC_PT * dSEC;
  double sB_res = o.reserveDM_PT       * dRES;
  double sB_mnt = o.maintenanceDM_PT   * dMNT;

  // --- Exudation guarded via polymorphic getter (only FineRoot returns >0) ---
	double sA_exu = 0.0, sB_exu = 0.0;
	double exuPT  = o.getExudationPT();   // mg C per step; 0 for non-root organs
	if (exuPT > 0.0 && !Double.isNaN(exuPT)) {
    double fEXU = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, o.km_res);
    double dEXU = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, o.km_res);
		sA_exu = exuPT * (fEXU - cp * dEXU);
		sB_exu = exuPT * dEXU;
	}

	/*
	 * Signed direct transport is not a Michaelis-Menten sink. Fruit overrides
	 * supply its exact value and analytical dM/dPhi at this Taylor point.
	 */
	double massFlowPhi = (cp > CT_CP_MIN) ? cp : CT_CP_MIN;
	double massFlowSugar = sugarFromCp(massFlowPhi);
	double massFlow0 = o.getDirectMassFlowCarbon(massFlowSugar);
	double massFlowB = o.getDirectMassFlowDerivativePhi(
		massFlowPhi, massFlowSugar);
	if (Double.isNaN(massFlow0) || Double.isInfinite(massFlow0)) massFlow0 = 0.0;
	if (Double.isNaN(massFlowB) || Double.isInfinite(massFlowB)) massFlowB = 0.0;
	double massFlowA = massFlow0 - massFlowPhi * massFlowB;

	// sums
	double sinkA = (sA_pri + sA_sec + sA_res + sA_mnt + sA_exu
		+ massFlowA);
	double sinkB = (sB_pri + sB_sec + sB_res + sB_mnt + sB_exu
		+ massFlowB);

  // Combine sources + sinks, convert units once here
  o.sink_source_a = mgTogram * (sinkA + loadA);
  o.sink_source_b = mgTogram * (sinkB + loadB);

  if (debug_CT && (o instanceof Trunk || o instanceof Cordon || o instanceof StructuralRoot || o instanceof FruitService)) {
    println(o.getClass().getSimpleName()
      + " loadPT=" + o.loading_PT
      + " priPT="  + o.structureDM_PRI_PT
      + " secPT="  + o.structureDM_SEC_PT
      + " resPT="  + o.reserveDM_PT
      + " mntPT="  + o.maintenanceDM_PT
      + " cp="     + cp
      + " | loadA=" + loadA + " loadB=" + loadB
      + " | priA="  + sA_pri + " priB=" + sB_pri
      + " | secA="  + sA_sec + " secB=" + sB_sec
      + " | resA="  + sA_res + " resB=" + sB_res
      + " | mntA="  + sA_mnt + " mntB=" + sB_mnt
	  + " | massFlowA=" + massFlowA + " massFlowB=" + massFlowB
      + " | A=" + (sinkA + loadA)
      + " | B=" + (sinkB + loadB));
  }
}


/* Carbon Dynamics Phases defined as groups --------------------------------- */

//group Linearise: // linearise equations for sinks/sources 
//left to right
/**
 * Linearises the sink/source relationships for all {@link GrowingOrgan} instances in the graph.
 * <p>
 * This method:
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Resets diagnostic accumulators for A/B coefficients and fluxes.</li>
 *   <li>Invokes {@link #lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan)} on each organ to compute per-organ
 *       linearised coefficients for sink and source terms.</li>
 *   <li>Accumulates totals per organ type for debugging and diagnostics.</li>
 *   <li>Optionally prints the per-class totals if {@code debug_CT} is enabled.</li>
 * </ul>
 * The linearisation results are stored in each organ's {@code sink_source_a} and {@code sink_source_b}
 * fields, and also copied to {@code branch_flux_a} and {@code branch_flux_b}.
 */
static void linearise(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx,
    CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.leafA = ctx.leafB = ctx.leafJ = 0.0;
  ctx.petioleA = ctx.petioleB = ctx.petioleJ = 0.0;
  ctx.shootA = ctx.shootB = ctx.shootJ = 0.0;
  ctx.fineRootA = ctx.fineRootB = ctx.fineRootJ = 0.0;
  ctx.structuralRootA = ctx.structuralRootB = ctx.structuralRootJ = 0.0;
  ctx.fruitA = ctx.fruitB = ctx.fruitJ = 0.0;
  ctx.flowerA = ctx.flowerB = ctx.flowerJ = 0.0;

  for (int organIndex = 0; organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    lineariseOrgan(organ);
    organ.branch_flux_a = organ.sink_source_a;
    organ.branch_flux_b = organ.sink_source_b;
    double jTerm = organ.sink_source_a + organ.sink_source_b * organ.cpt;
    if (organ instanceof Leaf) {
      ctx.leafA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.leafB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.leafJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof Petiole) {
      ctx.petioleA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.petioleB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.petioleJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof Internode) {
      ctx.shootA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.shootB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.shootJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof FineRoot) {
      ctx.fineRootA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.fineRootB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.fineRootJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof StructuralRoot) {
      ctx.structuralRootA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.structuralRootB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.structuralRootJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof FruitService) {
      ctx.fruitA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.fruitB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.fruitJ += jTerm;
    } else if (organ instanceof Flower) {
      ctx.flowerA += organ.sink_source_a; ctx.flowerB += organ.sink_source_b; ctx.flowerJ += jTerm;
    }
  }

  if (debug_CT) {
    println(
        "DEBUG A/B by class   A            B            j\n" +
        "Leaf:        " + ctx.leafA + "  " + ctx.leafB + "  " + ctx.leafJ + "\n" +
        "Petiole:     " + ctx.petioleA + "  " + ctx.petioleB + "  " + ctx.petioleJ + "\n" +
        "Shoot(core): " + ctx.shootA + "  " + ctx.shootB + "  " + ctx.shootJ + "\n" +
        "FineRoot:    " + ctx.fineRootA + "  " + ctx.fineRootB + "  " + ctx.fineRootJ + "\n" +
        "StrRoot:     " + ctx.structuralRootA + "  " + ctx.structuralRootB + "  " + ctx.structuralRootJ + "\n" +
        "Fruit:       " + ctx.fruitA + "  " + ctx.fruitB + "  " + ctx.fruitJ + "\n" +
        "Flower:      " + ctx.flowerA + "  " + ctx.flowerB + "  " + ctx.flowerJ);
  }
}


/* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
//UpdateBranchFlux:	
//backward transport, folding all the carbon flux
/* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
// UpdateBranchFlux:
// Backward transport, folding all the carbon flux

/**
 * Propagate branch fluxes upstream along each axis (shoot) by folding from
 * terminal {@code Internode}s toward the plant base, aggregating contributions
 * from local sinks and multiple child organs (petioles, fruits, and lateral
 * internodes). Cordon and Trunk nodes are covered implicitly because they
 * subclass {@code Internode}.
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose</b>:
 * Compute per-axis carbon transport terms {@code branch_flux_a} and
 * {@code branch_flux_b} by:
 * <ol>
 *   <li>Seeding the deepest internode in each order with its own sink,
 *       plus all child petiole/fruit fluxes;</li>
 *   <li>Walking upstream via {@code getPredecessor()}, accumulating the
 *       downstream branch (from the node just processed) plus local child
 *       organ fluxes at each upstream internode (including Cordon/Trunk).</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <p><b>Key features</b>:
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Performs per-order, per-rank folding of internodes.</li>
 *   <li>Handles structural root folding layer-by-layer via parent links.</li>
 *   <li>Combines both shoot and root carbon fluxes at the PlantBase.</li>
 *   <li>Uses {@code foldTick} to prevent multiple writes within one iteration.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Integration</b>:
 * Call this after all sink/source terms are computed for the current time step
 * and before any reporting or forward transport operations.
 * 
 * @since 2025-08
 */

// Add a global flag to control debug_CT output


/** Return -1 for no root parent and -2 when the two root pointers disagree. */
static long ctStructuralRootParentId(
    StructuralRoot rootNode, int plantNumber) {
  long resolvedId = -1L;
  long firstCandidateId = rootNode.parentID;
  if (firstCandidateId > 0) {
    Object firstCandidate = graph().getNodeForId(firstCandidateId);
    if (firstCandidate instanceof StructuralRoot
        && ((StructuralRoot) firstCandidate).plantNumber == plantNumber) {
      resolvedId = firstCandidateId;
    }
  }
  long secondCandidateId = rootNode.verticalParentID;
  if (secondCandidateId > 0 && secondCandidateId != resolvedId) {
    Object secondCandidate = graph().getNodeForId(secondCandidateId);
    if (secondCandidate instanceof StructuralRoot
        && ((StructuralRoot) secondCandidate).plantNumber == plantNumber) {
      if (resolvedId > 0) return -2L;
      resolvedId = secondCandidateId;
    }
  }
  return resolvedId;
}

static boolean ctRootPointsToPlantBase(StructuralRoot rootNode,
    PlantBase pb) {
  return rootNode.parentID == pb.getId()
      || rootNode.verticalParentID == pb.getId();
}

/** Whether the explicit StructuralRoot backlink contains one child graph id. */
static boolean ctStructuralRootHasChildId(
    StructuralRoot rootNode, long childId) {
  if (rootNode == null || childId <= 0) return false;
  int childIndex;
  int childCount = rootNode.getChildStructuralRootCount();
  for (childIndex = 0; childIndex < childCount; childIndex++) {
    if (rootNode.getChildStructuralRootIdAt(childIndex) == childId) {
      return true;
    }
  }
  return false;
}

/**
 * Fold one validated simple-root layer from raw local/lateral/distal terms.
 * FineRoot currently has r=xp=0, but its inherited transform is retained so
 * future resistance can be added without changing the assembly contract.
 */
static boolean foldSimpleRootSegment(StructuralRoot rootNode,
    FineRoot fineRootNode, StructuralRoot deeperRoot,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  if (rootNode == null || fineRootNode == null || ctx == null) return false;
  if (rootNode.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
    ctx.simpleRootDoubleFoldCount++;
    ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = false;
    println("ERROR(CT-SIMPLE-ROOT-DOUBLE-FOLD): layer="
        + rootNode.layer + " id=" + rootNode.getId()
        + " foldStep=" + ctx.foldStep);
    return false;
  }
  if (fineRootNode.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
    ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = false;
    println("ERROR(CT-SIMPLE-FINE-ROOT-DOUBLE-FOLD): layer="
        + fineRootNode.layer + " id=" + fineRootNode.getId()
        + " foldStep=" + ctx.foldStep);
    return false;
  }
  if (deeperRoot != null && deeperRoot.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep) {
    ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = false;
    println("ERROR(CT-SIMPLE-ROOT-ORDER): child layer="
        + deeperRoot.layer + " id=" + deeperRoot.getId()
        + " was not folded before parent layer=" + rootNode.layer
        + " id=" + rootNode.getId());
    return false;
  }

  fineRootNode.branch_flux_a = fineRootNode.sink_source_a;
  fineRootNode.branch_flux_b = fineRootNode.sink_source_b;
  fineRootNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
  fineRootNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;

  double sumA = rootNode.sink_source_a + fineRootNode.branch_flux_a;
  double sumB = rootNode.sink_source_b + fineRootNode.branch_flux_b;
  fineRootNode.foldRecv++;
  if (deeperRoot != null) {
    sumA += deeperRoot.branch_flux_a;
    sumB += deeperRoot.branch_flux_b;
    deeperRoot.foldRecv++;
  }

  rootNode.branch_flux_a = sumA;
  rootNode.branch_flux_b = sumB;
  rootNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
  rootNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  ctx.simpleFineRootFolded++;
  ctx.simpleStructuralRootFolded++;
  return true;
}

/**
 * Deterministic deepest-to-surface fold for useComplexRoot == false only.
 * The existing topology-aware complex-root branch remains separate below.
 */
static void foldSimpleRootLayers(PlantBase pb,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.simpleRootActive = true;
  ctx.simpleRootTopologyValid = topology.valid;
  ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = topology.valid;
  ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = topology.valid;
  ctx.simpleRootDoubleFoldCount = 0;
  ctx.simpleStructuralRootFolded = 0;
  ctx.simpleStructuralRootUnfolded = 0;
  ctx.simpleFineRootFolded = 0;
  ctx.simpleFineRootUnfolded = 0;
  ctx.simpleRootMinLayer = topology.simpleRootMinLayer;
  ctx.simpleRootMaxLayer = topology.simpleRootMaxLayer;
  ctx.simpleRootLayerCount = topology.simpleStructuralRoots.size();
  ctx.simpleStructuralRootExpected = topology.simpleStructuralRoots.size();
  ctx.simpleFineRootExpected = topology.simpleFineRoots.size();

  StructuralRoot deeperRoot = null;
  for (int foldIndex = 0;
      foldIndex < topology.simpleRootFoldOrder.size(); foldIndex++) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.simpleRootFoldOrder.get(foldIndex);
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.fineRootByLayer.get(
        Integer.valueOf(rootNode.layer));
    if (!foldSimpleRootSegment(rootNode, fineNode, deeperRoot, ctx)) {
      ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = false;
    }
    deeperRoot = rootNode;
  }
  if (topology.simpleBasalRoot != null
      && topology.simpleBasalRoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
    topology.simpleBasalRoot.foldRecv++;
  } else {
    ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = false;
  }
  ctx.simpleRootFoldValid = ctx.simpleRootFoldValid
      && ctx.simpleRootDoubleFoldCount == 0
      && ctx.simpleStructuralRootFolded == ctx.simpleStructuralRootExpected
      && ctx.simpleFineRootFolded == ctx.simpleFineRootExpected;
}

static int foldTick = 0;
static void updateBranchFlux(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) [
  {
    long scopedOrganCount = count((* foldScope:GrowingOrgan, (
      foldScope.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedOrganCount > 0) {
      int persistedFoldStep = max((* persistedFold:GrowingOrgan, (
        persistedFold.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[lastFoldStep]);
      if (foldTick < persistedFoldStep) foldTick = persistedFoldStep;
    }
    ctx.foldStep = ++foldTick;
  }

  foldReset:GrowingOrgan, (
    foldReset.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    foldReset.foldRecv = 0;
    foldReset.foldExpect = 1;
    foldReset.ctTransportOwnerId = -1L;
    foldReset.ctTransportOwnerCount = 0;
  }

  /* Resolve distinct topological Petiole owners before any Leaf is folded. */
  petioleOwner:Petiole (-->){1,5} ownedLeaf:Leaf, (
    petioleOwner.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    && ownedLeaf.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    if (ownedLeaf.ctTransportOwnerId != petioleOwner.getId()) {
      if (ownedLeaf.ctTransportOwnerCount == 0) {
        ownedLeaf.ctTransportOwnerId = petioleOwner.getId();
      } else if (debug_CT) {
        println("ERROR(CT-LEAF): ambiguous Petiole topology"
            + " leafId=" + ownedLeaf.getId()
            + " firstOwner=" + ownedLeaf.ctTransportOwnerId
            + " additionalOwner=" + petioleOwner.getId()
            + " plantNumber=" + ownedLeaf.plantNumber);
      }
      ownedLeaf.ctTransportOwnerCount++;
    }
  }

  /* Resolve distinct pointer owners for FineRoot terminals. */
  fineOwner:StructuralRoot, (
    fineOwner.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    for (FineRoot ownedFineRoot : (* ownedFineQuery:FineRoot, (
        ownedFineQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        && (ownedFineQuery.parentID == fineOwner.getId()
            || fineOwner.frID == ownedFineQuery.getId())
    ) *)) {
      if (ownedFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerId != fineOwner.getId()) {
        if (ownedFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerCount == 0) {
          ownedFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerId = fineOwner.getId();
        }
        ownedFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerCount++;
      }
    }
  }

  /* Leaf is transported through one topological Petiole, or directly via its Internode pointer. */
  petioleNode:Petiole, (
    petioleNode.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    double sumA = petioleNode.sink_source_a;
    double sumB = petioleNode.sink_source_b;
    for (Leaf leafChild : (* petioleNode (-->){1,5} petioleLeafQuery:Leaf *)) {
      if (leafChild.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) continue;
      if (leafChild.ctTransportOwnerCount == 1
          && leafChild.ctTransportOwnerId == petioleNode.getId()
          && leafChild.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep) {
        sumA += leafChild.branch_flux_a;
        sumB += leafChild.branch_flux_b;
        leafChild.foldRecv++;
        leafChild.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
        if (debug_CT && petioleNode.rank != leafChild.rank) {
          println("WARN(CT-LEAF): rank mismatch retained by topology"
              + " petioleId=" + petioleNode.getId()
              + " petioleRank=" + petioleNode.rank
              + " leafId=" + leafChild.getId()
              + " leafRank=" + leafChild.rank);
        }
      } else if (debug_CT && leafChild.ctTransportOwnerCount > 1) {
        println("ERROR(CT-LEAF): ambiguous Petiole owners"
            + " leafId=" + leafChild.getId()
            + " ownerCount=" + leafChild.ctTransportOwnerCount);
      }
    }
    petioleNode.branch_flux_a = sumA;
    petioleNode.branch_flux_b = sumB;
    petioleNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    petioleNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  /* Flowers and FineRoots have real transport resistance and are transformed once. */
  flowerNode:Flower, (
    flowerNode.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    flowerNode.branch_flux_a = flowerNode.sink_source_a;
    flowerNode.branch_flux_b = flowerNode.sink_source_b;
    flowerNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    flowerNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  fineRootNode:FineRoot, (
    useComplexRoot == true
    && fineRootNode.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    fineRootNode.branch_flux_a = fineRootNode.sink_source_a;
    fineRootNode.branch_flux_b = fineRootNode.sink_source_b;
    fineRootNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    fineRootNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  /* Above-ground axes: collect every pointer-owned child, then transform once. */
  {
    long internodeCount = count((* shootCount:Internode, (
      shootCount.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (internodeCount > 0) {
      int minOrder = min((* shootMinOrder:Internode, (
        shootMinOrder.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[order]);
      int maxOrder = max((* shootMaxOrder:Internode, (
        shootMaxOrder.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[order]);
      for (int shootOrder = maxOrder; shootOrder >= minOrder; shootOrder--) {
        if (count((* shootAtOrder:Internode, (
          shootAtOrder.order == shootOrder
          && shootAtOrder.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        ) *)) == 0) continue;
        int minRank = min((* shootMinRank:Internode, (
          shootMinRank.order == shootOrder
          && shootMinRank.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        ) *)[rank]);
        int maxRank = max((* shootMaxRank:Internode, (
          shootMaxRank.order == shootOrder
          && shootMaxRank.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        ) *)[rank]);
        for (int shootRank = maxRank; shootRank >= minRank; shootRank--) {
          [
            axisNode:Internode, (
              axisNode.order == shootOrder && axisNode.rank == shootRank
              && axisNode.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            ) ::> {
              double sumA = axisNode.sink_source_a;
              double sumB = axisNode.sink_source_b;

              for (Internode childAxis : (* childAxisQuery:Internode, (
                  childAxisQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
                  && childAxisQuery.parentID == axisNode.getId()
              ) *)) {
                if (childAxis.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
                  sumA += childAxis.branch_flux_a;
                  sumB += childAxis.branch_flux_b;
                  childAxis.foldRecv++;
                } else if (debug_CT) {
                  println("ERROR(FOLD): child axis not ready childId="
                      + childAxis.getId() + " parentId=" + axisNode.getId());
                }
              }

              for (Petiole childPetiole : (* childPetioleQuery:Petiole, (
                  childPetioleQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
                  && childPetioleQuery.parentID == axisNode.getId()
              ) *)) {
                if (childPetiole.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
                  sumA += childPetiole.branch_flux_a;
                  sumB += childPetiole.branch_flux_b;
                  childPetiole.foldRecv++;
                }
              }

              for (FruitService childFruit : (* childFruitQuery:FruitService, (
                  childFruitQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
                  && childFruitQuery.parentID == axisNode.getId()
              ) *)) {
                sumA += childFruit.branch_flux_a;
                sumB += childFruit.branch_flux_b;
                childFruit.foldRecv++;
                childFruit.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
              }

              for (Flower childFlower : (* childFlowerQuery:Flower, (
                  childFlowerQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
                  && childFlowerQuery.parentID == axisNode.getId()
              ) *)) {
                if (childFlower.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
                  sumA += childFlower.branch_flux_a;
                  sumB += childFlower.branch_flux_b;
                  childFlower.foldRecv++;
                }
              }

              /* Direct-Internode Leaf fallback is used only when no Petiole path exists. */
              for (Leaf directLeaf : (* directLeafQuery:Leaf, (
                  directLeafQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
                  && directLeafQuery.parentID == axisNode.getId()
              ) *)) {
                if (directLeaf.ctTransportOwnerCount == 0) {
                  sumA += directLeaf.branch_flux_a;
                  sumB += directLeaf.branch_flux_b;
                  directLeaf.foldRecv++;
                  directLeaf.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
                }
              }

              axisNode.branch_flux_a = sumA;
              axisNode.branch_flux_b = sumB;
              axisNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
              axisNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /* Complex-root CT folding intentionally unchanged here.
   * It requires a separate topology-aware audit. */
  {
    if (useComplexRoot == true) {
    long rootCount = count((* rootCountQuery:StructuralRoot, (
      rootCountQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    for (int rootPass = 0; rootPass <= rootCount; rootPass++) {
      [
        rootNode:StructuralRoot, (
          rootNode.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
          && rootNode.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep
        ) ::> {
          long rootParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
              rootNode, pb.plantNumber);
          boolean ready = rootParentId != -2L;
          double sumA = rootNode.sink_source_a;
          double sumB = rootNode.sink_source_b;

          for (StructuralRoot childRoot : (* rootChildQuery:StructuralRoot, (
              rootChildQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
          ) *)) {
            long childParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
                childRoot, pb.plantNumber);
            if (childParentId == rootNode.getId()) {
              if (childRoot.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep) {
                ready = false;
              } else {
                sumA += childRoot.branch_flux_a;
                sumB += childRoot.branch_flux_b;
              }
            }
          }

          if (ready) {
            for (FineRoot childFineRoot : (* rootFineQuery:FineRoot, (
                rootFineQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            ) *)) {
              if (childFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerCount == 1
                  && childFineRoot.ctTransportOwnerId == rootNode.getId()) {
                if (childFineRoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
                  sumA += childFineRoot.branch_flux_a;
                  sumB += childFineRoot.branch_flux_b;
                  childFineRoot.foldRecv++;
                } else {
                  ready = false;
                }
              }
            }
          }

          if (ready) {
            rootNode.branch_flux_a = sumA;
            rootNode.branch_flux_b = sumB;
            rootNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
            rootNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
            for (StructuralRoot contributedChild : (* contributedRootQuery:StructuralRoot, (
                contributedRootQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            ) *)) {
              long contributedParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
                  contributedChild, pb.plantNumber);
              if (contributedParentId == rootNode.getId()) {
                contributedChild.foldRecv++;
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }

    double rootA = 0.0;
    double rootB = 0.0;
    int minRootLayer = 0;
    if (rootCount > 0) {
      minRootLayer = min((* rootMinLayerQuery:StructuralRoot, (
        rootMinLayerQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[layer]);
    }
    for (StructuralRoot basalRoot : (* basalRootQuery:StructuralRoot, (
        basalRootQuery.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)) {
      long basalParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
          basalRoot, pb.plantNumber);
      boolean isBasal = basalParentId == -1L
          && (ctRootPointsToPlantBase(basalRoot, pb)
              || basalRoot.layer == minRootLayer);
      if (isBasal && basalRoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
        rootA += basalRoot.branch_flux_a;
        rootB += basalRoot.branch_flux_b;
        basalRoot.foldRecv++;
      }
    }

    Internode basalShoot = pb.getChildInternode();
    if (basalShoot != null && basalShoot.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) {
      basalShoot = null;
    }
    double shootA = 0.0;
    double shootB = 0.0;
    if (basalShoot != null && basalShoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
      shootA = basalShoot.branch_flux_a;
      shootB = basalShoot.branch_flux_b;
      basalShoot.foldRecv++;
    }
    pb.branch_flux_a = rootA + shootA;
    pb.branch_flux_b = rootB + shootB;
    }
  }

  {
    ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount = count((* foldTotal:GrowingOrgan, (
      foldTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount = count((* foldComplete:GrowingOrgan, (
      foldComplete.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      && foldComplete.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep
      && foldComplete.foldRecv == foldComplete.foldExpect
    ) *));
    ctx.foldCoverageComplete = ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount
        == ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount;
    if (debug_CT) {
      println("FOLD COVERAGE total=" + ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount
          + "/" + ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount
          + " leaf=" + count((* foldLeaf:Leaf, (foldLeaf.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldLeaf.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldLeaf.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldLeafTotal:Leaf, (foldLeafTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " petiole=" + count((* foldPetiole:Petiole, (foldPetiole.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldPetiole.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldPetiole.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldPetioleTotal:Petiole, (foldPetioleTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " shoot=" + count((* foldShoot:Internode, (foldShoot.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldShoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldShoot.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldShootTotal:Internode, (foldShootTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " fruit=" + count((* foldFruit:FruitService, (foldFruit.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldFruit.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldFruit.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldFruitTotal:FruitService, (foldFruitTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " flower=" + count((* foldFlower:Flower, (foldFlower.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldFlower.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldFlower.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldFlowerTotal:Flower, (foldFlowerTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " structuralRoot=" + count((* foldRoot:StructuralRoot, (foldRoot.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldRoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldRoot.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldRootTotal:StructuralRoot, (foldRootTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " fineRoot=" + count((* foldFine:FineRoot, (foldFine.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && foldFine.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && foldFine.foldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* foldFineTotal:FineRoot, (foldFineTotal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *)));
    }
  }

  missingFold:GrowingOrgan, (
    debug_CT && missingFold.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    && (missingFold.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep
        || missingFold.foldRecv != missingFold.foldExpect)
  ) ::> {
    println("ERROR(CT-FOLD-COVERAGE): id=" + missingFold.getId()
        + " class=" + missingFold.getClass().getSimpleName()
        + " parentID=" + missingFold.parentID
        + " rank=" + missingFold.rank
        + " order=" + missingFold.order
        + " plantNumber=" + missingFold.plantNumber
        + " foldRecv=" + missingFold.foldRecv);
  }
]

/** O(N+E) CT9-compatible fold used by the production simple-root solve. */
static void updateBranchFluxCached(PlantBase pb,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  // Complex-root topology remains on its unchanged legacy path in this branch.
  if (useComplexRoot == true) {
    updateBranchFlux(pb, ctx);
    return;
  }

  if (foldTick < topology.maxLastFoldStep) {
    foldTick = topology.maxLastFoldStep;
  }
  ctx.foldStep = ++foldTick;
  ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount = topology.growingOrgans.size();
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    organ.foldRecv = 0;
    organ.foldExpect = 1;
  }

  for (Object petioleKeyObject : topology.petiolesById.keySet()) {
    Long petioleKey = (Long) petioleKeyObject;
    Petiole petioleNode = (Petiole) topology.petiolesById.get(petioleKey);
    double rawA = petioleNode.sink_source_a;
    double rawB = petioleNode.sink_source_b;
    ArrayList ownedLeaves = ctList(topology.leavesByPetiole, petioleKey);
    for (int leafIndex = 0; leafIndex < ownedLeaves.size(); leafIndex++) {
      Leaf leafNode = (Leaf) ownedLeaves.get(leafIndex);
      rawA += leafNode.branch_flux_a;
      rawB += leafNode.branch_flux_b;
      leafNode.foldRecv++;
      leafNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
      if (debug_CT && petioleNode.rank != leafNode.rank) {
        println("WARN(CT-LEAF): rank mismatch retained by topology"
            + " petioleId=" + petioleNode.getId()
            + " petioleRank=" + petioleNode.rank
            + " leafId=" + leafNode.getId()
            + " leafRank=" + leafNode.rank);
      }
    }
    petioleNode.branch_flux_a = rawA;
    petioleNode.branch_flux_b = rawB;
    petioleNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    petioleNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  for (Object flowerKeyObject : topology.flowersById.keySet()) {
    Flower flowerNode = (Flower) topology.flowersById.get((Long) flowerKeyObject);
    flowerNode.branch_flux_a = flowerNode.sink_source_a;
    flowerNode.branch_flux_b = flowerNode.sink_source_b;
    flowerNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    flowerNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  for (int orderIndex = 0;
      orderIndex < topology.shootPostOrder.size(); orderIndex++) {
    Long axisKey = (Long) topology.shootPostOrder.get(orderIndex);
    Internode axisNode = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(axisKey);
    double sumA = axisNode.sink_source_a;
    double sumB = axisNode.sink_source_b;

    ArrayList childAxes = ctList(
        topology.childInternodesByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0; childIndex < childAxes.size(); childIndex++) {
      Long childKey = (Long) childAxes.get(childIndex);
      Internode child = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(childKey);
      if (child.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep) {
        ctx.foldCoverageComplete = false;
        if (debug_CT) println("ERROR(FOLD): child axis not ready childId="
            + child.getId() + " parentId=" + axisNode.getId());
        continue;
      }
      sumA += child.branch_flux_a;
      sumB += child.branch_flux_b;
      child.foldRecv++;
    }

    ArrayList petioleChildren = ctList(
        topology.childPetiolesByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < petioleChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      Petiole child = (Petiole) petioleChildren.get(childIndex);
      sumA += child.branch_flux_a;
      sumB += child.branch_flux_b;
      child.foldRecv++;
    }
    ArrayList fruitChildren = ctList(
        topology.childFruitsByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < fruitChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      FruitService child = (FruitService) fruitChildren.get(childIndex);
      sumA += child.branch_flux_a;
      sumB += child.branch_flux_b;
      child.foldRecv++;
      child.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
    }
    ArrayList flowerChildren = ctList(
        topology.childFlowersByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < flowerChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      Flower child = (Flower) flowerChildren.get(childIndex);
      sumA += child.branch_flux_a;
      sumB += child.branch_flux_b;
      child.foldRecv++;
    }
    ArrayList directLeaves = ctList(
        topology.directLeavesByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < directLeaves.size(); childIndex++) {
      Leaf child = (Leaf) directLeaves.get(childIndex);
      sumA += child.branch_flux_a;
      sumB += child.branch_flux_b;
      child.foldRecv++;
      child.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
    }

    axisNode.branch_flux_a = sumA;
    axisNode.branch_flux_b = sumB;
    axisNode.Update_Branch_Flux();
    axisNode.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
  }

  foldSimpleRootLayers(pb, ctx, topology);
  double rootA = (topology.simpleBasalRoot == null)
      ? 0.0 : topology.simpleBasalRoot.branch_flux_a;
  double rootB = (topology.simpleBasalRoot == null)
      ? 0.0 : topology.simpleBasalRoot.branch_flux_b;
  double shootA = 0.0;
  double shootB = 0.0;
  for (int basalIndex = 0;
      basalIndex < topology.basalShootIds.size(); basalIndex++) {
    Long basalKey = (Long) topology.basalShootIds.get(basalIndex);
    Internode basalShoot = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(basalKey);
    if (basalShoot.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
      shootA += basalShoot.branch_flux_a;
      shootB += basalShoot.branch_flux_b;
      basalShoot.foldRecv++;
    }
  }
  pb.branch_flux_a = rootA + shootA;
  pb.branch_flux_b = rootB + shootB;

  ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount = 0;
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    if (organ.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep
        && organ.foldRecv == organ.foldExpect) {
      ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount++;
    } else if (debug_CT) {
      println("ERROR(CT-FOLD-COVERAGE): id=" + organ.getId()
          + " class=" + organ.getClass().getSimpleName()
          + " parentID=" + organ.parentID
          + " foldRecv=" + organ.foldRecv);
    }
  }
  ctx.foldCoverageComplete = ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount
      == ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount;
  if (debug_CT) println("FOLD COVERAGE total="
      + ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount + "/" + ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount);
}



/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

//group UpdateCarbonPotentialUnfold:

/**
 * UpdateCarbonPotential: UNFOLD from plant base to all child organs
 * 
 * <p><b>Purpose:</b> Calculates the carbon potential (cpb/cpt) of all transport-linked organs
 * from the source (PlantBase) outward to sinks. Each organ's cpt is computed from its upstream cpb
 * using its flux values and resistance parameters (r, xp), enforcing directionality and conservation.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Method:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>PlantBase is seeded with cp = -A/B.</li>
 *   <li>Trunk and basal StructuralRoot are initialized from PB.cpt.</li>
 *   <li>StructuralRoots unfold by layer (deep to surface), via parent–child link.</li>
 *   <li>Shoots unfold from small → large internode order, rank-wise, using child lists.</li>
 *   <li>Petioles and Fruits are pushed similarly from Internode parent.</li>
 *   <li>Leaf cp is synced from petiole.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Debug control:</b> All output respects a global <code>debug_CT</code> flag.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */
static int unfoldTick = 0;            // monotonic counter

static boolean isFiniteCarbonValue(double v) {
    return !Double.isNaN(v) && !Double.isInfinite(v);
}

static boolean isValidPhi(double phi) {
    return isFiniteCarbonValue(phi) && phi >= CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

static double safePhi(double value) {
    return isValidPhi(value) ? value : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

static double validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(double phi) {
    if (!isValidPhi(phi)) return CT_PHI_FLOOR;
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(phi);
    return (isFiniteCarbonValue(sugar) && sugar >= 0.0) ? phi : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

/** Read the explicit accepted-hour marker with legacy saved-graph fallback. */
static boolean hasAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(PlantBase pb) {
    if (pb == null) return false;
    try {
        return pb.ctHasAcceptedHourlyState;
    } catch (NoSuchFieldError compatibilityError) {
        return false;
    }
}

/** Write the explicit accepted-hour marker with legacy saved-graph fallback. */
static void setAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(PlantBase pb,
        boolean accepted) {
    if (pb == null) return;
    try {
        pb.ctHasAcceptedHourlyState = accepted;
    } catch (NoSuchFieldError compatibilityError) {
        // Compatibility with legacy saved graphs that predate this state flag.
    }
}

/** Existing CT initialization seed, with only the existing numerical floor as fallback. */
static double carbonTransportInitializationPhi() {
    return isValidPhi(SOURCEcp) ? SOURCEcp : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

/**
 * Make the first pre-solve state internally consistent before it is snapshotted.
 * This is initialization recovery, not a biological sugar-concentration floor.
 */
static void prepareInitialCarbonTransportSnapshotState(PlantBase pb) {
    double initialPhi = pb.cpt;
    if (!isValidPhi(initialPhi)) {
        initialPhi = isValidPhi(pb.cpb)
            ? pb.cpb : carbonTransportInitializationPhi();
    }
    double initialSugar = sugarFromCp(initialPhi);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(initialSugar) || initialSugar <= 0.0) {
        initialPhi = carbonTransportInitializationPhi();
        initialSugar = sugarFromCp(initialPhi);
    }
    pb.cpb = initialPhi;
    pb.cpt = initialPhi;
    pb.sugarConcentration_phloem = initialSugar;
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre)
            || pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre <= 0.0) {
        pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre = initialSugar;
    }

    double organInitializationPhi = carbonTransportInitializationPhi();
    for (GrowingOrgan initialOrgan : (* initialStateOrgan:GrowingOrgan, (
        initialStateOrgan.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)) {
        double distalPhi = isValidPhi(initialOrgan.cpt)
            ? initialOrgan.cpt
            : (isValidPhi(initialOrgan.cpb)
                ? initialOrgan.cpb : organInitializationPhi);
        double basalPhi = isValidPhi(initialOrgan.cpb)
            ? initialOrgan.cpb : distalPhi;
        initialOrgan.cpb = basalPhi;
        initialOrgan.cpt = distalPhi;
    }

    updateResistence(pb);
    pb.updateCTRs(Math.sqrt(2.0 * pb.cpt));
}

static double retainPlantBasePhi(PlantBase pb, double fallbackPhi, int reason) {
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = 1;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = reason;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount++;
    return fallbackPhi;
}

static double clampCtDampingFactor(double alpha) {
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(alpha)) return CT_DAMPING_INITIAL;
    return Math.max(CT_DAMPING_MIN, Math.min(CT_DAMPING_MAX, alpha));
}

static double underRelaxPlantBasePhi(double previousPhi, double rawPhi, double alpha) {
    double previous = validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(previousPhi);
    double raw = validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(rawPhi);
    double accepted = previous + clampCtDampingFactor(alpha) * (raw - previous);
    return validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(accepted);
}

static void markInvalidUnfoldTrial(CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    if (ctx == null) return;
    ctx.invalidUnfoldTrial = true;
    ctx.invalidUnfoldTrialCount++;
    ctx.totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount++;
    ctx.converged = false;
}

/** Claim exactly one transport parent for an unfold write in the current pass. */
static boolean claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(GrowingOrgan organ, long ownerId,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    if (organ == null || ctx == null) return false;
    if (organ.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep) {
        organ.unfoldRecv++;
        if (debug_CT) {
            println("ERROR(CT-UNFOLD): ambiguous owner id=" + organ.getId()
                + " class=" + organ.getClass().getSimpleName()
                + " firstOwner=" + organ.lastWriterId
                + " secondOwner=" + ownerId);
        }
        return false;
    }
    organ.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
    organ.lastWriterId = ownerId;
    organ.unfoldRecv = 1;
    return true;
}

/**
 * Under-relax one raw child-organ Phi trial without destroying a valid iterate.
 * Invalid raw or accepted values retain the previous finite Phi and invalidate
 * the complete nonlinear pass. The numerical floor is initialization/recovery
 * state only, when no valid previous Phi exists.
 */
static double underRelaxOrganPhi(double previousPhi, double trialPhi,
        double alpha, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    double previous = isValidPhi(previousPhi) ? previousPhi : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
    if (!isValidPhi(trialPhi)) {
        markInvalidUnfoldTrial(ctx);
        return previous;
    }
    double accepted = previous
        + clampCtDampingFactor(alpha) * (trialPhi - previous);
    if (!isValidPhi(accepted)) {
        markInvalidUnfoldTrial(ctx);
        return previous;
    }
    return accepted;
}

/** Unfold one validated simple StructuralRoot and its same-layer FineRoot. */
static boolean unfoldSimpleRootSegment(StructuralRoot rootNode,
        FineRoot fineRootNode, double upstreamPhi, long upstreamOwnerId,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    if (rootNode == null || fineRootNode == null || ctx == null) return false;
    if (!claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(rootNode, upstreamOwnerId, ctx)) {
        ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = false;
        return false;
    }
    rootNode.cpb = upstreamPhi;
    double rootTrialPhi = rootNode.cpb
        * (1.0 - rootNode.branch_flux_b * rootNode.r)
        - rootNode.branch_flux_a * rootNode.r - rootNode.xp;
    rootNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
        rootNode.cpt, rootTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
    ctx.simpleStructuralRootUnfolded++;

    if (!claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
        fineRootNode, rootNode.getId(), ctx)) {
        ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = false;
        return false;
    }
    fineRootNode.cpb = rootNode.cpt;
    double fineTrialPhi = fineRootNode.cpb
        * (1.0 - fineRootNode.branch_flux_b * fineRootNode.r)
        - fineRootNode.branch_flux_a * fineRootNode.r
        - fineRootNode.xp;
    fineRootNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
        fineRootNode.cpt, fineTrialPhi,
        ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
    ctx.simpleFineRootUnfolded++;
    return true;
}

/** Deterministic surface-to-deep unfold for useComplexRoot == false only. */
static void unfoldSimpleRootLayers(PlantBase pb,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = ctx.simpleRootTopologyValid
      && ctx.simpleRootFoldValid;
  StructuralRoot previousRoot = null;
  for (int unfoldIndex = 0;
      unfoldIndex < topology.simpleRootUnfoldOrder.size(); unfoldIndex++) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.simpleRootUnfoldOrder.get(unfoldIndex);
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.fineRootByLayer.get(
        Integer.valueOf(rootNode.layer));
    double upstreamPhi = (previousRoot == null) ? pb.cpt : previousRoot.cpt;
    long upstreamOwnerId = (previousRoot == null)
        ? pb.getId() : previousRoot.getId();
    if (!ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid
        || !unfoldSimpleRootSegment(rootNode, fineNode,
            upstreamPhi, upstreamOwnerId, ctx)) {
      ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = false;
    }
    previousRoot = rootNode;
  }
  ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid = ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid
      && ctx.simpleStructuralRootUnfolded == ctx.simpleStructuralRootExpected
      && ctx.simpleFineRootUnfolded == ctx.simpleFineRootExpected;
}

static double adaptCtDampingFactor(double alpha, double previousMerit, double currentMerit) {
    double nextAlpha = clampCtDampingFactor(alpha);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(currentMerit) || currentMerit < 0.0) {
        return Math.max(CT_DAMPING_MIN, 0.5 * nextAlpha);
    }
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(previousMerit) || previousMerit < 0.0) {
        return nextAlpha;
    }
    if (currentMerit > 1.05 * previousMerit) {
        return Math.max(CT_DAMPING_MIN, 0.5 * nextAlpha);
    }
    if (currentMerit < 0.7 * previousMerit) {
        return Math.min(CT_DAMPING_MAX, 1.25 * nextAlpha);
    }
    if (currentMerit <= previousMerit) {
        return Math.min(CT_DAMPING_MAX, nextAlpha + 0.05);
    }
    return nextAlpha;
}

static void resetCarbonTransportPassState(CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    ctx.convergenceError = 0.0;
    ctx.relativeFluxError = 0.0;
    ctx.oldFluxMagnitude = 0.0;
    ctx.newFluxMagnitude = 0.0;
    ctx.invalidUnfoldTrial = false;
    ctx.invalidUnfoldTrialCount = 0;
}

static double ctNormalizedError(double absoluteError, double scale) {
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(absoluteError) || absoluteError < 0.0) {
        return Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
    }
    double safeScale = isFiniteCarbonValue(scale) ? Math.max(scale, 1e-12) : 1e-12;
    double relativeError = absoluteError / safeScale;
    // The solve accepts either criterion, so its merit is the better normalized one.
    return Math.min(absoluteError / CT_ABS_FLUX_TOL,
        relativeError / CT_REL_FLUX_TOL);
}

static boolean ctMixedErrorConverged(double absoluteError, double scale) {
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(absoluteError) || absoluteError < 0.0) {
        return false;
    }
    double safeScale = isFiniteCarbonValue(scale) ? Math.max(scale, 1e-12) : 1e-12;
    return absoluteError <= CT_ABS_FLUX_TOL
        || absoluteError / safeScale <= CT_REL_FLUX_TOL;
}

static boolean ctSolveConverged(double absoluteFluxError, double fluxScale,
        double plantBaseResidual, double plantBaseScale) {
    return ctMixedErrorConverged(absoluteFluxError, fluxScale)
        && ctMixedErrorConverged(plantBaseResidual, plantBaseScale);
}

/** Exact active fruit unloading at one Phi without updating fruit state (mg C h-1). */
static double exactFruitActiveUnloadingMg(FruitService fruit, double phi) {
    if (fruit == null) return 0.0;
    double activity = fruit.shouldUsePreT1PotentialGrowth()
        ? 1.0 : SinkUnloading_fromSugar(phi, fruit.km_pri);
    double exactActive = fruit.structureDM_PRI_PT * activity;
    return isFiniteCarbonValue(exactActive) ? exactActive : 0.0;
}

/** Exact signed direct fruit mass flow at one Phi without committing references (mg C h-1). */
static double exactFruitMassFlowMg(FruitService fruit, double phi) {
    if (fruit == null) return 0.0;
    double exactMass = fruit.getDirectMassFlowCarbon(sugarFromCp(phi));
    return isFiniteCarbonValue(exactMass) ? exactMass : 0.0;
}

/** Exact intended CTRAM fruit import: active unloading plus signed mass flow (mg C h-1). */
static double exactFruitUnloadingMg(FruitService fruit, double phi) {
    return exactFruitActiveUnloadingMg(fruit, phi)
        + exactFruitMassFlowMg(fruit, phi);
}

/** Exact derivative of intended fruit import at one Phi (mg C h-1 per Phi). */
static double exactFruitUnloadingDerivativePhiMg(
        FruitService fruit, double phi) {
    if (fruit == null) return 0.0;
    double activeDerivative = fruit.shouldUsePreT1PotentialGrowth()
        ? 0.0
        : fruit.structureDM_PRI_PT
            * dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(phi, fruit.km_pri);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(phi);
    double massDerivative = fruit.getDirectMassFlowDerivativePhi(phi, sugar);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(activeDerivative)) activeDerivative = 0.0;
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(massDerivative)) massDerivative = 0.0;
    return activeDerivative + massDerivative;
}

static double solvePlantBasePhi(double branchA, double branchB,
        double previousPhi, PlantBase pb) {
    double fallbackPhi = validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(previousPhi);
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = 0;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = 0;
    pb.ctPlantBaseDenominator = branchB;

    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(branchA) || !isFiniteCarbonValue(branchB)) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 1);
    }
    if (Math.abs(branchB) <= CT_PB_B_ABS_MIN) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 2);
    }

    // Divide only after both folded coefficients and the denominator are accepted.
    double candidate = -branchA / branchB;
    if (!isValidPhi(candidate)) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 3);
    }

    double sugar = sugarFromCp(candidate);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 4);
    }
    return candidate;
}

static void installPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(PlantBase pb, double acceptedPhi) {
    pb.cpb = acceptedPhi;
    pb.cpt = acceptedPhi;
    pb.j = pb.branch_flux_a + pb.branch_flux_b * pb.cpt;
    pb.ctPlantBaseResidual = pb.j;
    pb.sugarConcentration_phloem = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
    pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre = pb.sugarConcentration_phloem;
}

static void applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(PlantBase pb, double alpha) {
    double previousPhi = pb.cpt;
    double rawPhi = solvePlantBasePhi(
        pb.branch_flux_a, pb.branch_flux_b, previousPhi, pb);
    installPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(pb,
        underRelaxPlantBasePhi(previousPhi, rawPhi, alpha));
}

static void applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(
        PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
    double previousPhi = pb.cpt;
    double rawPhi = solvePlantBasePhi(
        pb.branch_flux_a, pb.branch_flux_b, previousPhi, pb);
    double acceptedPhi = underRelaxPlantBasePhi(
        previousPhi, rawPhi, ctx.dampingFactor);
    installPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(pb, acceptedPhi);

    ctx.rawPlantBasePhi = rawPhi;
    ctx.acceptedPlantBasePhi = acceptedPhi;
    ctx.plantBaseResidual = Math.abs(pb.ctPlantBaseResidual);
    ctx.plantBaseScale = Math.max(Math.max(Math.abs(pb.branch_flux_a),
        Math.abs(pb.branch_flux_b * acceptedPhi)), 1e-12);
    ctx.plantBaseRelativeResidual = ctx.plantBaseResidual / ctx.plantBaseScale;
    ctx.plantBaseNormalizedError = ctNormalizedError(
        ctx.plantBaseResidual, ctx.plantBaseScale);
}

static void updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx)
[
  {
    long scopedOrganCount = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
      g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedOrganCount > 0) {
      int persistedUnfoldStep = max((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[lastUnfoldStep]);
      if (unfoldTick < persistedUnfoldStep) unfoldTick = persistedUnfoldStep;
    }
    ctx.unfoldStep = ++unfoldTick;
  }

  unfoldReset:GrowingOrgan, (
    unfoldReset.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    unfoldReset.unfoldRecv = 0;
    unfoldReset.lastWriterId = -1L;
  }

  {
    applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(pb, ctx);
    //println("pb.cpt: " + pb.cpt + " pb.sugarConcentration_phloem: " + pb.sugarConcentration_phloem);
    if (debug_CT) println("PB A=" + pb.branch_flux_a + " B=" + pb.branch_flux_b + " cpt=" + pb.cpt + " j=" + pb.j);
  }

// --- Legacy complex-root unfold plus shared basal shoot unfold ---
{
  if (useComplexRoot == true) {
  long rootCount = count((* unfoldRootCount:StructuralRoot, (
    unfoldRootCount.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *));
  int minRootLayer = 0;
  if (rootCount > 0) {
    minRootLayer = min((* unfoldRootMin:StructuralRoot, (
      unfoldRootMin.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[layer]);
  }

  java.util.ArrayList rootStack = new java.util.ArrayList();
  for (StructuralRoot basalRoot : (* unfoldBasalRoot:StructuralRoot, (
      unfoldBasalRoot.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)) {
    long basalParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
        basalRoot, pb.plantNumber);
    boolean isBasal = basalParentId == -1L
        && (ctRootPointsToPlantBase(basalRoot, pb)
            || basalRoot.layer == minRootLayer);
    if (isBasal && claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
        basalRoot, pb.getId(), ctx)) {
      basalRoot.cpb = pb.cpt;
      double basalTrialPhi = basalRoot.cpb
          * (1.0 - basalRoot.branch_flux_b * basalRoot.r)
          - basalRoot.branch_flux_a * basalRoot.r - basalRoot.xp;
      basalRoot.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
          basalRoot.cpt, basalTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      rootStack.add(basalRoot);
    }
  }

  while (!rootStack.isEmpty()) {
    StructuralRoot rootParent = (StructuralRoot)
        rootStack.remove(rootStack.size() - 1);
    for (StructuralRoot rootChild : (* unfoldRootChild:StructuralRoot, (
        unfoldRootChild.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)) {
      long childParentId = ctStructuralRootParentId(
          rootChild, pb.plantNumber);
      if (childParentId == rootParent.getId()
          && claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(rootChild, rootParent.getId(), ctx)) {
        rootChild.cpb = rootParent.cpt;
        double childTrialPhi = rootChild.cpb
            * (1.0 - rootChild.branch_flux_b * rootChild.r)
            - rootChild.branch_flux_a * rootChild.r - rootChild.xp;
        rootChild.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
            rootChild.cpt, childTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      rootStack.add(rootChild);
      }
    }
  }
  }

  Internode basalShoot = pb.getChildInternode();
  if (basalShoot != null && basalShoot.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) {
    basalShoot = null;
  }
  if (basalShoot != null && claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
      basalShoot, pb.getId(), ctx)) {
    basalShoot.cpb = pb.cpt;
    double shootTrialPhi = basalShoot.cpb
        * (1.0 - basalShoot.branch_flux_b * basalShoot.r)
        - basalShoot.branch_flux_a * basalShoot.r - basalShoot.xp;
    basalShoot.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
        basalShoot.cpt, shootTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
  }
}

// --- UNFOLD: StructuralRoot -> uniquely pointer-owned FineRoot ---
fineRootTerminal:FineRoot, (
  useComplexRoot == true
  && fineRootTerminal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
) ::> {
  if (fineRootTerminal.ctTransportOwnerCount == 1) {
    Object fineOwnerObject = graph().getNodeForId(
        fineRootTerminal.ctTransportOwnerId);
    if (fineOwnerObject instanceof StructuralRoot) {
    StructuralRoot rootOwner = (StructuralRoot) fineOwnerObject;
    if (rootOwner.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep
        && claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
            fineRootTerminal, rootOwner.getId(), ctx)) {
      fineRootTerminal.cpb = rootOwner.cpt;
      double fineTrialPhi = fineRootTerminal.cpb
          * (1.0 - fineRootTerminal.branch_flux_b * fineRootTerminal.r)
          - fineRootTerminal.branch_flux_a * fineRootTerminal.r
          - fineRootTerminal.xp;
      fineRootTerminal.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
          fineRootTerminal.cpt, fineTrialPhi,
          ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
    }
    }
  }
}


// Unfold the above-ground transport tree from low order/rank to its children.
  {
    long scopedInternodeCount = count((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedInternodeCount > 0) {
    int minOrder = min((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    int maxOrder = max((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    for (int o = minOrder; o <= maxOrder; o++) {
      if (count((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)) == 0) continue;
      int minRank = min((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);
      int maxRank = max((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);
      for (int r = minRank; r <= maxRank; r++) {
        [ parent:Internode, (
          parent.order == o && parent.rank == r &&
          parent.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        ) ::> {
          if (debug_CT) println("O" + o + " rank " + r + " id=" + parent.getId() + " cpb=" + parent.cpb + " cpt=" + parent.cpt);
          for (Internode ch : (* unfoldChildAxis:Internode, (
              unfoldChildAxis.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
              && unfoldChildAxis.parentID == parent.getId()
          ) *)) {
            if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(ch, parent.getId(), ctx)) {
              ch.cpb = parent.cpt;
              double childShootTrialPhi = ch.cpb * (1.0 - ch.branch_flux_b * ch.r)
                  - ch.branch_flux_a * ch.r - ch.xp;
              ch.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
                  ch.cpt, childShootTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child int id=" + ch.getId() + " cpb=" + ch.cpb + " cpt=" + ch.cpt);
            }
          }

          for (Petiole p : (* unfoldPetiole:Petiole, (
              unfoldPetiole.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
              && unfoldPetiole.parentID == parent.getId()
          ) *)) {
            if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(p, parent.getId(), ctx)) {
              p.cpb = parent.cpt;
              double petioleTrialPhi = p.cpb * (1.0 - p.branch_flux_b * p.r)
                  - p.branch_flux_a * p.r - p.xp;
              p.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
                  p.cpt, petioleTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child petiole id=" + p.getId() + " cpb=" + p.cpb + " cpt=" + p.cpt);
            }
          }

          for (FruitService f : (* unfoldFruit:FruitService, (
              unfoldFruit.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
              && unfoldFruit.parentID == parent.getId()
          ) *)) {
            if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(f, parent.getId(), ctx)) {
              f.cpb = parent.cpt;
              f.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
                  f.cpt, f.cpb, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
              if (debug_CT) 
              	  println("  -> child fruit id=" + f.getId() + " cpb=" + f.cpb + " cpt=" + f.cpt);
            }
          }
          
          for (Flower fl : (* unfoldFlower:Flower, (
              unfoldFlower.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
              && unfoldFlower.parentID == parent.getId()
          ) *)) {
            if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(fl, parent.getId(), ctx)) {
              fl.cpb = parent.cpt;
              double flowerTrialPhi = fl.cpb * (1.0 - fl.branch_flux_b * fl.r)
                  - fl.branch_flux_a * fl.r - fl.xp;
              fl.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
                  fl.cpt, flowerTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child flower id=" + fl.getId() + " cpb=" + fl.cpb + " cpt=" + fl.cpt);
            }
          }
          
        } ]
      }
    }
    }
  }

  /* Resolve each Leaf once. Rank mismatch is reported but never gates transport. */
  unfoldLeaf:Leaf, (
    unfoldLeaf.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::> {
    GrowingOrgan leafOwner = null;
    if (unfoldLeaf.ctTransportOwnerCount == 1) {
      Object leafOwnerObject = graph().getNodeForId(
          unfoldLeaf.ctTransportOwnerId);
      if (leafOwnerObject instanceof Petiole) {
        leafOwner = (Petiole) leafOwnerObject;
      }
    } else if (unfoldLeaf.ctTransportOwnerCount == 0) {
      Organ biologicalParent = unfoldLeaf.getParent();
      if (biologicalParent instanceof Internode
          && biologicalParent.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
        leafOwner = (Internode) biologicalParent;
      }
    }
    if (leafOwner != null
        && leafOwner.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep
        && claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
            unfoldLeaf, leafOwner.getId(), ctx)) {
      unfoldLeaf.cpb = leafOwner.cpt;
      unfoldLeaf.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
          unfoldLeaf.cpt, unfoldLeaf.cpb,
          ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      if (debug_CT && leafOwner instanceof Petiole
          && leafOwner.rank != unfoldLeaf.rank) {
        println("WARN(CT-LEAF): rank mismatch retained by topology"
            + " petioleId=" + leafOwner.getId()
            + " petioleRank=" + leafOwner.rank
            + " leafId=" + unfoldLeaf.getId()
            + " leafRank=" + unfoldLeaf.rank);
      }
    }
  }

  {
    ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount = count((* unfoldComplete:GrowingOrgan, (
      unfoldComplete.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      && unfoldComplete.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep
      && unfoldComplete.unfoldRecv == 1
    ) *));
    ctx.unfoldCoverageComplete = ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount
        == ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount;
    if (debug_CT) {
      println("UNFOLD COVERAGE total=" + ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount
          + "/" + ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount
          + " leaf=" + count((* unfoldLeafDone:Leaf, (unfoldLeafDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldLeafDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldLeafDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldLeafAll:Leaf, (unfoldLeafAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " petiole=" + count((* unfoldPetioleDone:Petiole, (unfoldPetioleDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldPetioleDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldPetioleDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldPetioleAll:Petiole, (unfoldPetioleAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " shoot=" + count((* unfoldShootDone:Internode, (unfoldShootDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldShootDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldShootDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldShootAll:Internode, (unfoldShootAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " fruit=" + count((* unfoldFruitDone:FruitService, (unfoldFruitDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldFruitDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldFruitDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldFruitAll:FruitService, (unfoldFruitAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " flower=" + count((* unfoldFlowerDone:Flower, (unfoldFlowerDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldFlowerDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldFlowerDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldFlowerAll:Flower, (unfoldFlowerAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " structuralRoot=" + count((* unfoldRootDone:StructuralRoot, (unfoldRootDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldRootDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldRootDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldRootAll:StructuralRoot, (unfoldRootAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *))
          + " fineRoot=" + count((* unfoldFineDone:FineRoot, (unfoldFineDone.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && unfoldFineDone.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && unfoldFineDone.unfoldRecv == 1) *))
          + "/" + count((* unfoldFineAll:FineRoot, (unfoldFineAll.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) *)));
    }
  }

  missingUnfold:GrowingOrgan, (
    debug_CT && missingUnfold.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    && (missingUnfold.lastUnfoldStep != ctx.unfoldStep
        || missingUnfold.unfoldRecv != 1)
  ) ::> {
    println("ERROR(CT-UNFOLD-COVERAGE): id=" + missingUnfold.getId()
        + " class=" + missingUnfold.getClass().getSimpleName()
        + " parentID=" + missingUnfold.parentID
        + " writerID=" + missingUnfold.lastWriterId
        + " rank=" + missingUnfold.rank
        + " order=" + missingUnfold.order
        + " plantNumber=" + missingUnfold.plantNumber
        + " unfoldRecv=" + missingUnfold.unfoldRecv);
  }

]

/** O(N+E) CT9-compatible unfold used by the production simple-root solve. */
static void updateCarbonPotentialCached(PlantBase pb,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  // Complex-root topology remains on its unchanged legacy path in this branch.
  if (useComplexRoot == true) {
    updateCarbonPotential(pb, ctx);
    return;
  }

  if (unfoldTick < topology.maxLastUnfoldStep) {
    unfoldTick = topology.maxLastUnfoldStep;
  }
  ctx.unfoldStep = ++unfoldTick;
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    organ.unfoldRecv = 0;
    organ.lastWriterId = -1L;
  }

  applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(pb, ctx);
  unfoldSimpleRootLayers(pb, ctx, topology);

  for (int orderIndex = 0;
      orderIndex < topology.shootPreOrder.size(); orderIndex++) {
    Long axisKey = (Long) topology.shootPreOrder.get(orderIndex);
    Internode axisNode = (Internode) topology.internodesById.get(axisKey);
    Long parentKey = (Long) topology.parentByInternode.get(axisKey);
    double upstreamPhi = pb.cpt;
    long ownerId = pb.getId();
    if (parentKey != null) {
      Internode parentNode = (Internode)
          topology.internodesById.get(parentKey);
      upstreamPhi = parentNode.cpt;
      ownerId = parentNode.getId();
    }
    if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(axisNode, ownerId, ctx)) {
      axisNode.cpb = upstreamPhi;
      double axisTrialPhi = axisNode.cpb
          * (1.0 - axisNode.branch_flux_b * axisNode.r)
          - axisNode.branch_flux_a * axisNode.r - axisNode.xp;
      axisNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
          axisNode.cpt, axisTrialPhi, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
    }

    ArrayList petioleChildren = ctList(
        topology.childPetiolesByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < petioleChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      Petiole petioleNode = (Petiole) petioleChildren.get(childIndex);
      if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
          petioleNode, axisNode.getId(), ctx)) {
        petioleNode.cpb = axisNode.cpt;
        double petioleTrialPhi = petioleNode.cpb
            * (1.0 - petioleNode.branch_flux_b * petioleNode.r)
            - petioleNode.branch_flux_a * petioleNode.r - petioleNode.xp;
        petioleNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
            petioleNode.cpt, petioleTrialPhi,
            ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      }
      ArrayList ownedLeaves = ctList(topology.leavesByPetiole,
          Long.valueOf(petioleNode.getId()));
      for (int leafIndex = 0; leafIndex < ownedLeaves.size(); leafIndex++) {
        Leaf leafNode = (Leaf) ownedLeaves.get(leafIndex);
        if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(
            leafNode, petioleNode.getId(), ctx)) {
          leafNode.cpb = petioleNode.cpt;
          leafNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
              leafNode.cpt, leafNode.cpb, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
        }
      }
    }

    ArrayList fruitChildren = ctList(
        topology.childFruitsByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < fruitChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      FruitService fruitNode = (FruitService) fruitChildren.get(childIndex);
      if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(fruitNode, axisNode.getId(), ctx)) {
        fruitNode.cpb = axisNode.cpt;
        fruitNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
            fruitNode.cpt, fruitNode.cpb, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      }
    }
    ArrayList flowerChildren = ctList(
        topology.childFlowersByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < flowerChildren.size(); childIndex++) {
      Flower flowerNode = (Flower) flowerChildren.get(childIndex);
      if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(flowerNode, axisNode.getId(), ctx)) {
        flowerNode.cpb = axisNode.cpt;
        double flowerTrialPhi = flowerNode.cpb
            * (1.0 - flowerNode.branch_flux_b * flowerNode.r)
            - flowerNode.branch_flux_a * flowerNode.r - flowerNode.xp;
        flowerNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
            flowerNode.cpt, flowerTrialPhi,
            ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      }
    }
    ArrayList directLeaves = ctList(
        topology.directLeavesByInternode, axisKey);
    for (int childIndex = 0;
        childIndex < directLeaves.size(); childIndex++) {
      Leaf leafNode = (Leaf) directLeaves.get(childIndex);
      if (claimCarbonUnfoldOwner(leafNode, axisNode.getId(), ctx)) {
        leafNode.cpb = axisNode.cpt;
        leafNode.cpt = underRelaxOrganPhi(
            leafNode.cpt, leafNode.cpb, ctx.dampingFactor, ctx);
      }
    }
  }

  ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount = 0;
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    if (organ.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && organ.unfoldRecv == 1) {
      ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount++;
    } else if (debug_CT) {
      println("ERROR(CT-UNFOLD-COVERAGE): id=" + organ.getId()
          + " class=" + organ.getClass().getSimpleName()
          + " parentID=" + organ.parentID
          + " writerID=" + organ.lastWriterId
          + " unfoldRecv=" + organ.unfoldRecv);
    }
  }
  ctx.unfoldCoverageComplete = ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount
      == ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount;
  if (debug_CT) println("UNFOLD COVERAGE total="
      + ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount + "/" + ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount);
}

/**
 * Root-only closure audit for the simple layered route (g C h-1).
 * This remains diagnostic and does not add a whole-plant convergence gate.
 */
static void updateSimpleRootClosureDiagnostics(
        PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) [
  {
    ctx.simpleRootLocalJ = 0.0;
    ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ = 0.0;
    ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual = 0.0;
    ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual = 0.0;
    if (useComplexRoot == false) {
      ctx.simpleRootLocalJ = sum((* simpleClosureSr:StructuralRoot, (
        simpleClosureSr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) + sum((* simpleClosureFr:FineRoot, (
        simpleClosureFr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]);
      StructuralRoot basalClosureRoot = first((* simpleClosureBasal:StructuralRoot, (
        simpleClosureBasal.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        && simpleClosureBasal.layer == ctx.simpleRootMinLayer
      ) *));
      if (basalClosureRoot != null) {
        ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ = basalClosureRoot.branch_flux_a
            + basalClosureRoot.branch_flux_b * pb.cpt;
      }
      ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual = ctx.simpleRootLocalJ
          - ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ;
      double simpleRootClosureScale = Math.max(Math.max(
          Math.abs(ctx.simpleRootLocalJ),
          Math.abs(ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ)), 1e-12);
      ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual = Math.abs(
          ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual) / simpleRootClosureScale;

      if (debug_CT) {
        int diagnosticLayer;
        for (diagnosticLayer = ctx.simpleRootMinLayer;
            diagnosticLayer <= ctx.simpleRootMaxLayer;
            diagnosticLayer++) {
          StructuralRoot diagnosticRoot = first((* simpleDiagSr:StructuralRoot, (
            simpleDiagSr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            && simpleDiagSr.layer == diagnosticLayer
          ) *));
          if (diagnosticRoot == null) continue;
          FineRoot diagnosticFine = first((* simpleDiagFr:FineRoot, (
            simpleDiagFr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            && simpleDiagFr.layer == diagnosticLayer
            && simpleDiagFr.parentID == diagnosticRoot.getId()
            && diagnosticRoot.frID == simpleDiagFr.getId()
          ) *));
          StructuralRoot diagnosticChild = first((* simpleDiagChild:StructuralRoot, (
            simpleDiagChild.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            && simpleDiagChild.layer == diagnosticLayer + 1
            && simpleDiagChild.parentID == diagnosticRoot.getId()
          ) *));
          Object diagnosticParentObject = (diagnosticRoot.parentID > 0)
              ? graph().getNodeForId(diagnosticRoot.parentID) : null;
          long diagnosticParentId = (diagnosticParentObject instanceof StructuralRoot)
              ? ((StructuralRoot) diagnosticParentObject).getId() : -1L;
          long diagnosticChildId = (diagnosticChild == null)
              ? -1L : diagnosticChild.getId();
          double diagnosticSrLocalJ = diagnosticRoot.j;
          double diagnosticFrLocalJ = (diagnosticFine == null)
              ? 0.0 : diagnosticFine.j;
          double diagnosticChildEntryJ = (diagnosticChild == null)
              ? 0.0 : diagnosticChild.branch_flux_a
                  + diagnosticChild.branch_flux_b * diagnosticChild.cpb;
          double diagnosticRawA = diagnosticRoot.sink_source_a
              + ((diagnosticFine == null) ? 0.0
                  : diagnosticFine.branch_flux_a)
              + ((diagnosticChild == null) ? 0.0
                  : diagnosticChild.branch_flux_a);
          double diagnosticRawB = diagnosticRoot.sink_source_b
              + ((diagnosticFine == null) ? 0.0
                  : diagnosticFine.branch_flux_b)
              + ((diagnosticChild == null) ? 0.0
                  : diagnosticChild.branch_flux_b);
          double diagnosticFoldedEntryJ = diagnosticRoot.branch_flux_a
              + diagnosticRoot.branch_flux_b * diagnosticRoot.cpb;
          double diagnosticLocalSubtreeJ = sum((* simpleDiagSubSr:StructuralRoot, (
            simpleDiagSubSr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            && simpleDiagSubSr.layer >= diagnosticLayer
          ) *)[j]) + sum((* simpleDiagSubFr:FineRoot, (
            simpleDiagSubFr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
            && simpleDiagSubFr.layer >= diagnosticLayer
          ) *)[j]);
          double diagnosticSubtreeResidual = diagnosticLocalSubtreeJ
              - diagnosticFoldedEntryJ;

          println("ROOT-CT layer=" + diagnosticLayer
              + " SR=" + diagnosticRoot.getId()
              + " FR=" + ((diagnosticFine == null) ? -1L : diagnosticFine.getId())
              + " parentSR=" + diagnosticParentId
              + " childSR=" + diagnosticChildId
              + " srLocalJ=" + diagnosticSrLocalJ
              + " frLocalJ=" + diagnosticFrLocalJ
              + " childFoldedEntryJ=" + diagnosticChildEntryJ
              + " rawA=" + diagnosticRawA
              + " rawB=" + diagnosticRawB
              + " foldedA=" + diagnosticRoot.branch_flux_a
              + " foldedB=" + diagnosticRoot.branch_flux_b
              + " cpb=" + diagnosticRoot.cpb
              + " cpt=" + diagnosticRoot.cpt
              + " foldedEntryJ=" + diagnosticFoldedEntryJ
              + " localSubtreeJ=" + diagnosticLocalSubtreeJ
              + " subtreeResidual=" + diagnosticSubtreeResidual);
        }
        println("ROOT-CT CLOSURE local=" + ctx.simpleRootLocalJ
            + " folded=" + ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ
            + " residual=" + ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual
            + " relative=" + ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual);
      }
    }
  }
]

/** --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * UpdateFlow — one Newton step that updates each organ’s linearized
 * source/sink flux j using the current local carbon potential (cpt).
 *
 * <p><b>What it does</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>For every GrowingOrgan <code>sd</code>, computes the new flux
 *       <code>new_j = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt</code>,
 *       i.e. the first-order (Taylor) linearization of the Michaelis–Menten
 *       sink/source function with respect to carbon potential Φ (stored here
 *       as <code>cpt</code> at the “top” side of the transport segment).</li>
 *   <li>Saves the residual <code>sd.err = new_j - sd.j</code> and accumulates
 *       it into the per-call convergence residual.</li>
 *   <li>Applies a small-current threshold <code>EPSILON</code> and clamps
 *       near-zero fluxes to 0 for numerical stability.</li>
 *   <li>Guards against invalid carbon potentials: if <code>cpt &lt; 0</code> or
 *       NaN/Inf, reset to a small positive value.</li>
 *   <li>Calls <code>derive()</code> to update derived state after flux changes.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Sign & units</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><code>sd.j</code> is the net <em>mass carbon transport</em> for that organ
 *       (gC·h⁻¹). Convention: <em>positive</em> j = unloading from phloem to the organ
 *       (sink); <em>negative</em> j = loading from organ to phloem (source).</li>
 *   <li><code>sd.sink_source_a</code>, <code>sd.sink_source_b</code> are the linear
 *       coefficients a, b from the Taylor expansion of the sink/source law
 *       around Φ₀, i.e. <code>j ≈ a + b Φ</code>.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Background</b>
 * In the coupled phloem/xylem transport (CT) model, we solve mass flux
 * using the “carbon potential” Φ ≝ c²/2 so that the transport law is linear
 * in dΦ/dx. Organs’ nonlinear sink/source laws are linearized as
 * <code>j = a + b Φ</code> for each iteration of the global solve.
 * See: definition of Φ and j, transport equation, and linearization of
 * sink functions with a and b. 
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
static void updateFlow(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx)
[
  {
    ctx.sumLeafStoredJ = ctx.sumLeafTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumPetioleStoredJ = ctx.sumPetioleTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumShootStoredJ = ctx.sumShootTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFruitStoredJ = ctx.sumFruitTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFlowerStoredJ = ctx.sumFlowerTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFineRootStoredJ = ctx.sumFineRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ = ctx.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFruitExactActive = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow = 0.0;
    ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading = 0.0;
    ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual = 0.0;
    ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = 0.0;
    ctx.maxFruitResidualOrganID = -1L;
    ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = 0.0;
    ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  }

  sd:GrowingOrgan, (
    sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::>
  {
    double new_j = 0.0;
    double old_j = isFiniteCarbonValue(sd.j) ? sd.j : 0.0;
    ctx.oldFluxMagnitude += Math.abs(old_j);

    if (sd.cpt >= 0.0 && !Double.isNaN(sd.cpt) && !Double.isInfinite(sd.cpt)) {
      // Linearized sink/source: j = a + b * Φ (Φ stored as cpt here)
      new_j = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt;

      if (isFiniteCarbonValue(new_j)) {
        // Residual for this organ and accumulate absolute error (g C h-1).
        sd.err = new_j - old_j;
        ctx.convergenceError += Math.abs(sd.err);
        // Threshold very small currents for stability.
        if (Math.abs(new_j) < EPSILON) {
          sd.j = 0.0;
        } else {
          sd.j = new_j;
        }
      } else {
        // Retain the last finite current-step iterate when reconstruction fails.
        sd.j = old_j;
        sd.err = 1.0;
        ctx.convergenceError += 1.0;
      }
    } else {
      // Invalid Phi: retain the finite flux and force rollback/retry; never floor
      // a failed current iterate here because that would destroy accepted history.
      sd.j = old_j;
      sd.err = 1.0;
      ctx.convergenceError += 1.0;
      markInvalidUnfoldTrial(ctx);
    }
    ctx.newFluxMagnitude += Math.abs(sd.j);

    double localTaylorJ = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt;
    if (sd instanceof Leaf) {
      ctx.sumLeafStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumLeafTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (sd instanceof Petiole) {
      ctx.sumPetioleStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumPetioleTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (sd instanceof Internode || sd instanceof Cordon || sd instanceof Trunk) {
      ctx.sumShootStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumShootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (sd instanceof FruitService) {
      ctx.sumFruitStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumFruitTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
      FruitService fruit = (FruitService) sd;
      double finalPhi = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, fruit.cpt);
      double exactActiveG = mgTogram
          * exactFruitActiveUnloadingMg(fruit, finalPhi);
      double exactMassG = mgTogram
          * exactFruitMassFlowMg(fruit, finalPhi);
      double exactUnloadingG = exactActiveG + exactMassG;
      ctx.sumFruitExactActive += exactActiveG;
      ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow += exactMassG;
      ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading += exactUnloadingG;
      ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading += mgTogram * fruit.unloading;

      double fruitResidual = fruit.j - exactUnloadingG;
      double fruitScale = Math.max(Math.max(
          Math.abs(fruit.j), Math.abs(exactUnloadingG)), 1e-12);
      double fruitRelativeResidual = Math.abs(fruitResidual) / fruitScale;
      if (Math.abs(fruitResidual) > ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual) {
        ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual = Math.abs(fruitResidual);
        ctx.maxFruitResidualOrganID = fruit.getId();
      }
      ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = Math.max(
          ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual,
          fruitRelativeResidual);

      /* Non-committing Taylor reconstruction exactly at the final local Phi. */
      double exactDerivativeG = mgTogram
          * exactFruitUnloadingDerivativePhiMg(fruit, finalPhi);
      double finalPointA = exactUnloadingG - finalPhi * exactDerivativeG;
      double finalPointB = exactDerivativeG;
      double finalPointResidual = finalPointA + finalPointB * finalPhi
          - exactUnloadingG;
      double finalPointScale = Math.max(Math.abs(exactUnloadingG), 1e-12);
      ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = Math.max(
          ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual, Math.abs(finalPointResidual));
      ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual = Math.max(
          ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual,
          Math.abs(finalPointResidual) / finalPointScale);
    } else if (sd instanceof Flower) {
      ctx.sumFlowerStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumFlowerTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (sd instanceof FineRoot) {
      ctx.sumFineRootStoredJ += sd.j; ctx.sumFineRootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (sd instanceof StructuralRoot) {
      ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ += sd.j;
      ctx.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    }

    
    if (debug_CT) {
      println(
        "sd." + sd.nodeNumber +
        " j="   + sd.j +
        " cpt=" + sd.cpt +
        " cpb=" + sd.cpb +
        " sink_a=" + sd.sink_source_a +
        " sink_b=" + sd.sink_source_b
      );
    }
  }


 {
  updateSimpleRootClosureDiagnostics(pb, ctx);
  ctx.sumLocalJ = sum((* closureOrgan:GrowingOrgan, (
    closureOrgan.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)[j]);
  ctx.pbFoldedJ = pb.j;
  ctx.closureResidual = ctx.sumLocalJ - ctx.pbFoldedJ;
  ctx.closureScale = Math.max(Math.max(
      ctx.newFluxMagnitude, Math.abs(ctx.pbFoldedJ)), 1e-12);
  ctx.relativeClosureResidual = Math.abs(ctx.closureResidual)
      / ctx.closureScale;
  ctx.closureNormalizedError = ctNormalizedError(
      Math.abs(ctx.closureResidual), ctx.closureScale);

  ctx.totalLoading = Math.abs(sum((* closureLoad:GrowingOrgan, (
    closureLoad.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && closureLoad.j < 0.0
  ) *)[j]));
  ctx.totalUnloading = sum((* closureUnload:GrowingOrgan, (
    closureUnload.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber && closureUnload.j > 0.0
  ) *)[j]);
  ctx.netFluxResidual = ctx.totalLoading - ctx.totalUnloading;
  ctx.relativeNetFluxResidual = Math.abs(ctx.netFluxResidual)
      / Math.max(Math.max(ctx.totalLoading, ctx.totalUnloading), 1e-12);
  ctx.netFluxIdentityResidual = ctx.netFluxResidual + ctx.sumLocalJ;
  /* Fruit-local exactness is diagnostic-only until reduced-scenario evidence
   * establishes a safe magnitude; it does not participate in ctConverged. */
  ctx.fruitLinearizationResidual = ctx.sumFruitStoredJ
      - ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading;
  ctx.fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = Math.abs(
      ctx.fruitLinearizationResidual) / Math.max(Math.max(
          Math.abs(ctx.sumFruitStoredJ),
          Math.abs(ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading)), 1e-12);
  ctx.fruitStoredVsExactResidual = ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading
      - ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading;

  ctx.fluxScale = Math.max(Math.max(
      ctx.newFluxMagnitude, ctx.oldFluxMagnitude), 1e-12);
  ctx.relativeFluxError = ctx.convergenceError / ctx.fluxScale;
  ctx.fluxNormalizedError = ctNormalizedError(
      ctx.convergenceError, ctx.fluxScale);
  ctx.nonlinearMerit = Math.max(
      ctx.fluxNormalizedError, ctx.plantBaseNormalizedError);
  ctx.converged = ctSolveConverged(
      ctx.convergenceError, ctx.fluxScale,
      ctx.plantBaseResidual, ctx.plantBaseScale);
  if (ctx.invalidUnfoldTrial
      || (ctx.simpleRootActive
          && (!ctx.simpleRootTopologyValid
              || !ctx.simpleRootFoldValid
              || !ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid))) {
    ctx.nonlinearMerit = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
    ctx.converged = false;
  }

  if (debug_CT) {
 //if(true) {
    println(
      "Iter " + ctx.iterationCount +
      " | sumj=" + sum((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | sum|j|=" + sum(Math.abs((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j])) +
      " | internode=" + sum((* g:Internode, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | structuralRoot=" + sum((* g:StructuralRoot, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | Leaf=" + sum((* g:Leaf, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | Fruit=" + sum((* g:FruitService, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j])
    );
    
   // After updateFlow() + convergence, add:

  println("CLOSURE CHECK  sum(j_organs)=" + ctx.sumLocalJ
        + "  pb.j=" + ctx.pbFoldedJ
        + "  sumLocalJ-pb.j=" + ctx.closureResidual
        + "  relative=" + ctx.relativeClosureResidual);
  println("FRUIT CHECK  sumFruitJ=" + ctx.sumFruitStoredJ
        + "  exact=" + ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading
        + "  storedUnloading=" + ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading
        + "  exactActive=" + ctx.sumFruitExactActive
        + "  exactMassFlow=" + ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow
        + "  relative=" + ctx.fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual);
 
  }
 }
]

private static void updateSimpleRootClosureDiagnosticsCached(
    PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx,
    CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.simpleRootLocalJ = 0.0;
  ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ = 0.0;
  ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual = 0.0;
  ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual = 0.0;
  if (useComplexRoot == true) return;
  for (int rootIndex = 0;
      rootIndex < topology.simpleStructuralRoots.size(); rootIndex++) {
    StructuralRoot rootNode = (StructuralRoot)
        topology.simpleStructuralRoots.get(rootIndex);
    FineRoot fineNode = (FineRoot) topology.simpleFineRoots.get(rootIndex);
    ctx.simpleRootLocalJ += rootNode.j + fineNode.j;
  }
  if (topology.simpleBasalRoot != null) {
    ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ = topology.simpleBasalRoot.branch_flux_a
        + topology.simpleBasalRoot.branch_flux_b * pb.cpt;
  }
  ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual = ctx.simpleRootLocalJ
      - ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ;
  double scale = Math.max(Math.max(
      Math.abs(ctx.simpleRootLocalJ),
      Math.abs(ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ)), 1e-12);
  ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual = Math.abs(
      ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual) / scale;
}

/** O(N) flow reconstruction and closure accumulation without graph queries. */
static void updateFlowCached(PlantBase pb,
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.sumLeafStoredJ = ctx.sumLeafTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumPetioleStoredJ = ctx.sumPetioleTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumShootStoredJ = ctx.sumShootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFruitStoredJ = ctx.sumFruitTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFlowerStoredJ = ctx.sumFlowerTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFineRootStoredJ = ctx.sumFineRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ = ctx.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ = 0.0;
  ctx.sumLocalJ = 0.0;
  ctx.totalLoading = 0.0;
  ctx.totalUnloading = 0.0;

  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    double oldJ = isFiniteCarbonValue(organ.j) ? organ.j : 0.0;
    ctx.oldFluxMagnitude += Math.abs(oldJ);
    double newJ = oldJ;
    if (isFiniteCarbonValue(organ.cpt) && organ.cpt >= 0.0) {
      double candidateJ = organ.sink_source_a
          + organ.sink_source_b * organ.cpt;
      if (isFiniteCarbonValue(candidateJ)) {
        organ.err = candidateJ - oldJ;
        ctx.convergenceError += Math.abs(organ.err);
        newJ = (Math.abs(candidateJ) < EPSILON) ? 0.0 : candidateJ;
      } else {
        organ.err = 1.0;
        ctx.convergenceError += 1.0;
      }
    } else {
      organ.err = 1.0;
      ctx.convergenceError += 1.0;
      markInvalidUnfoldTrial(ctx);
    }
    organ.j = newJ;
    ctx.newFluxMagnitude += Math.abs(newJ);
    ctx.sumLocalJ += newJ;
    if (newJ > 0.0) ctx.totalUnloading += newJ;
    else if (newJ < 0.0) ctx.totalLoading += -newJ;

    double localTaylorJ = organ.sink_source_a
        + organ.sink_source_b * organ.cpt;
    if (organ instanceof Leaf) {
      ctx.sumLeafStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumLeafTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof Petiole) {
      ctx.sumPetioleStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumPetioleTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof Internode) {
      ctx.sumShootStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumShootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof FruitService) {
      ctx.sumFruitStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumFruitTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof Flower) {
      ctx.sumFlowerStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumFlowerTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof FineRoot) {
      ctx.sumFineRootStoredJ += newJ; ctx.sumFineRootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    } else if (organ instanceof StructuralRoot) {
      ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ += newJ;
      ctx.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ += localTaylorJ;
    }
  }

  updateSimpleRootClosureDiagnosticsCached(pb, ctx, topology);
  ctx.pbFoldedJ = pb.j;
  ctx.closureResidual = ctx.sumLocalJ - ctx.pbFoldedJ;
  ctx.closureScale = Math.max(Math.max(
      ctx.newFluxMagnitude, Math.abs(ctx.pbFoldedJ)), 1e-12);
  ctx.relativeClosureResidual = Math.abs(ctx.closureResidual)
      / ctx.closureScale;
  ctx.closureNormalizedError = ctNormalizedError(
      Math.abs(ctx.closureResidual), ctx.closureScale);
  ctx.netFluxResidual = ctx.totalLoading - ctx.totalUnloading;
  ctx.relativeNetFluxResidual = Math.abs(ctx.netFluxResidual)
      / Math.max(Math.max(ctx.totalLoading, ctx.totalUnloading), 1e-12);
  ctx.netFluxIdentityResidual = ctx.netFluxResidual + ctx.sumLocalJ;
  ctx.fluxScale = Math.max(Math.max(
      ctx.newFluxMagnitude, ctx.oldFluxMagnitude), 1e-12);
  ctx.relativeFluxError = ctx.convergenceError / ctx.fluxScale;
  ctx.fluxNormalizedError = ctNormalizedError(
      ctx.convergenceError, ctx.fluxScale);
  ctx.nonlinearMerit = Math.max(
      ctx.fluxNormalizedError, ctx.plantBaseNormalizedError);
  ctx.converged = ctSolveConverged(
      ctx.convergenceError, ctx.fluxScale,
      ctx.plantBaseResidual, ctx.plantBaseScale);
  if (ctx.invalidUnfoldTrial
      || !ctx.foldCoverageComplete || !ctx.unfoldCoverageComplete
      || (ctx.simpleRootActive
          && (!ctx.simpleRootTopologyValid
              || !ctx.simpleRootFoldValid
              || !ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid))) {
    ctx.nonlinearMerit = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
    ctx.converged = false;
  }

  if (debug_CT) {
    println("Iter " + ctx.iterationCount
        + " | sumj=" + ctx.sumLocalJ
        + " | sum|j|=" + ctx.newFluxMagnitude
        + " | internode=" + ctx.sumShootStoredJ
        + " | structuralRoot=" + ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ
        + " | Leaf=" + ctx.sumLeafStoredJ
        + " | Fruit=" + ctx.sumFruitStoredJ);
  }
}

/** Expensive exact fruit checks are evaluated once for the final trial state. */
static void updateFinalFruitCarbonDiagnostics(
    CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFruitExactActive = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow = 0.0;
  ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading = 0.0;
  ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual = 0.0;
  ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  ctx.maxFruitResidualOrganID = -1L;
  ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = 0.0;
  ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual = 0.0;
  for (Object fruitKeyObject : topology.fruitsById.keySet()) {
    FruitService fruit = (FruitService)
        topology.fruitsById.get((Long) fruitKeyObject);
    double finalPhi = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, fruit.cpt);
    double exactActiveG = mgTogram
        * exactFruitActiveUnloadingMg(fruit, finalPhi);
    double exactMassG = mgTogram
        * exactFruitMassFlowMg(fruit, finalPhi);
    double exactUnloadingG = exactActiveG + exactMassG;
    ctx.sumFruitExactActive += exactActiveG;
    ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow += exactMassG;
    ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading += exactUnloadingG;
    ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading += mgTogram * fruit.unloading;
    double fruitResidual = fruit.j - exactUnloadingG;
    double fruitScale = Math.max(Math.max(
        Math.abs(fruit.j), Math.abs(exactUnloadingG)), 1e-12);
    if (Math.abs(fruitResidual) > ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual) {
      ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual = Math.abs(fruitResidual);
      ctx.maxFruitResidualOrganID = fruit.getId();
    }
    ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = Math.max(
        ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual,
        Math.abs(fruitResidual) / fruitScale);

    double exactDerivativeG = mgTogram
        * exactFruitUnloadingDerivativePhiMg(fruit, finalPhi);
    double finalPointA = exactUnloadingG - finalPhi * exactDerivativeG;
    double finalPointResidual = finalPointA
        + exactDerivativeG * finalPhi - exactUnloadingG;
    double finalPointScale = Math.max(Math.abs(exactUnloadingG), 1e-12);
    ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = Math.max(
        ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual, Math.abs(finalPointResidual));
    ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual = Math.max(
        ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual,
        Math.abs(finalPointResidual) / finalPointScale);
  }
  ctx.fruitLinearizationResidual = ctx.sumFruitStoredJ
      - ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading;
  ctx.fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual = Math.abs(
      ctx.fruitLinearizationResidual) / Math.max(Math.max(
          Math.abs(ctx.sumFruitStoredJ),
          Math.abs(ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading)), 1e-12);
  ctx.fruitStoredVsExactResidual = ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading
      - ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading;
}


/**
 * Refresh transport resistances and related parameters per organ.
 *
 * <p>Derives phloem carbon concentration {@code c = sqrt(2*cpt)} and invokes
 * {@code updateCTRs(c)} to refresh local resistance {@code r}, osmotic terms, and
 * any transport coefficients dependent on concentration.</p>
 *
 * @implNote The method name is kept as {@code updateResistence()} for backward compatibility.
 * @since 2025-08
 */


static void updateResistence(PlantBase pb)
[
 
	 g:GrowingOrgan, (
	   g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 ) ::>
	{
	  if (isValidPhi(g.cpt)) {
	    double carbon = Math.sqrt(2.0 * g.cpt);
	    g.updateCTRs(carbon);
	  }
	  //test xp
	 // g.xp = 0;
	}
	
]

/** Per-iteration resistance refresh over the cached organ list. */
static void updateResistenceCached(CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan organ = (GrowingOrgan) topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    if (isValidPhi(organ.cpt)) {
      organ.updateCTRs(Math.sqrt(2.0 * organ.cpt));
    }
  }
}
/**
 * Update organ-level carbon status after the transport solve.
 *
 * <p><b>Actions</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Compute phloem carbon concentration and sugar units from {@code cpt}.</li>
 *   <li>Re-evaluate loading, leakage, and unloading terms in sugar space.</li>
 *   <li>Store {@code Cflux = j / mgTogram} for reporting (guard NaN).</li>
 *   <li>Refresh transport coefficients via {@code updateCTRs(carbon)}.</li>
 *   <li>Compute Munch counter flow {@code Mcf} using branch flux and local concentration.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Guards</b> — NaNs in branch flux or Mcf are replaced with small defaults.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */

static void updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase pb)
[
	//group develop 
	//{ double maxCp = max((*S *)[cpb]);}
	 
	 g:GrowingOrgan, (
	   g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 ) ::> {
		  double carbon = Math.sqrt(2.0 * g.cpt);
		  double sugar = convertPhloemCtoSugar(carbon);
		  
		  g.updateCarbonAllocation(sugar);
		  
		  g.Cflux = g.j * 1/mgTogram;	
		  if(Double.isNaN(g.Cflux)) g.Cflux = 1e-6;
		  //  s.cpt = s.cpb = maxCp;
		   
		  //s.cpb = s.cpt = max();  
		  g.updateCTRs(carbon);
		
		  // Effect of phloem flux on hydraulic flow: Munch counter flow (following Equation 5) 
		  //checked the original code McF do use cpb in the calculation. 
		  double branchj = g.branch_flux_a + g.branch_flux_b * g.cpb;
		  if(Double.isNaN(branchj)) { branchj = 1e-5;}
		 
		  g.Mcf = MolalVolumeSucrose * branchj - branchj / carbon;
		 
		  if(Double.isNaN(g.Mcf)) g.Mcf = 0;
		}
		
	 {
	 	pb.updateCarbonPartition();
	 }
		
		
]

/** Capture the last accepted hourly transport and transient allocation state. */
static CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshotCarbonTransportState(PlantBase pb) {
  if (pb == null) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Carbon transport snapshot requires PlantBase.");
  }
  CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshot =
      new CarbonTransportStateSnapshot(pb);
  for (GrowingOrgan transportOrgan : (* snapshotOrgan:GrowingOrgan, (
      snapshotOrgan.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)) {
    snapshot.organStates.add(new CarbonTransportOrganState(transportOrgan));
  }
  return snapshot;
}

/** Cached production overload: no graph query during the hourly solve. */
static CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshotCarbonTransportState(
    PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  if (pb == null) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Carbon transport snapshot requires PlantBase.");
  }
  CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshot =
      new CarbonTransportStateSnapshot(pb);
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan transportOrgan = (GrowingOrgan)
        topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    snapshot.organStates.add(new CarbonTransportOrganState(transportOrgan));
  }
  return snapshot;
}

/** Restore accepted state and rebuild concentration-dependent resistance. */
static void restoreCarbonTransportState(PlantBase pb,
        CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshot) {
  if (pb == null || snapshot == null || snapshot.plantBase != pb) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
        "Carbon transport restore requires the matching PlantBase snapshot.");
  }
  int stateCount = snapshot.organStates.size();
  for (int stateIndex = 0; stateIndex < stateCount; stateIndex++) {
    CarbonTransportOrganState organState =
        (CarbonTransportOrganState) snapshot.organStates.get(stateIndex);
    organState.restore();
  }
  snapshot.restorePlantBase();

  // Phi is authoritative. Reconstruct the reporting sugar instead of trusting
  // a cached value that may be zero or stale in an older accepted snapshot.
  if (isValidPhi(pb.cpt)) {
    double restoredSugar = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
    if (isFiniteCarbonValue(restoredSugar) && restoredSugar > 0.0) {
      pb.sugarConcentration_phloem = restoredSugar;
      if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre)
          || pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre <= 0.0) {
        pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre = restoredSugar;
      }
    }
  }

  // updateResistence() is the existing source of truth for r/xp. Recompute it
  // after restoring Phi so retry never starts from failed-iteration coefficients.
  updateResistence(pb);
  if (isValidPhi(pb.cpt)) {
    pb.updateCTRs(Math.sqrt(2.0 * pb.cpt));
  }
}

static boolean shouldStartCarbonTransportRetry(
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  return ctx != null && !ctx.converged && ctx.maxIterationReached
      && !ctx.retryUsed;
}

/** A complete finite normal trial is a safer retry seed than bootstrap. */
static boolean shouldWarmStartCarbonTransportRetry(
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  return ctx != null && ctx.failedTrialCaptured
      && ctx.totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount == 0;
}

static CarbonTransportSolveContext createCarbonTransportRetryContext(
        CarbonTransportSolveContext failedNormalContext) {
  CarbonTransportSolveContext retryContext =
      new CarbonTransportSolveContext();
  retryContext.dampingFactor = CT_RETRY_DAMPING_INITIAL;
  retryContext.retryUsed = true;
  retryContext.finalIterationLimit = CT_RETRY_MAX_ITERATIONS;
  if (failedNormalContext != null) {
    retryContext.totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount =
        failedNormalContext.totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount;
    retryContext.failedTrialCaptured =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialCaptured;
    retryContext.failedTrialPlantBasePhi =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialPlantBasePhi;
    retryContext.failedTrialPlantBaseSugar =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialPlantBaseSugar;
    retryContext.failedTrialMinSugar =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialMinSugar;
    retryContext.failedTrialMaxSugar =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialMaxSugar;
    retryContext.failedTrialMeanSugar =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialMeanSugar;
    retryContext.failedTrialMerit =
        failedNormalContext.failedTrialMerit;
  }
  return retryContext;
}

/** Retain the last complete finite nonlinear trial before any rollback. */
static void captureFailedCarbonTransportTrial(PlantBase pb,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  if (pb == null || ctx == null || ctx.converged
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(pb.cpt) || pb.cpt < 0.0
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(ctx.nonlinearMerit)
      || ctx.nonlinearMerit < 0.0) return;

  double plantBaseSugar = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
  if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(plantBaseSugar) || plantBaseSugar < 0.0) return;

  int finiteOrganCount = 0;
  double minSugar = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  double maxSugar = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;
  double sugarSum = 0.0;
  for (GrowingOrgan finiteTrialOrgan : (* failedTrialOrgan:GrowingOrgan, (
      failedTrialOrgan.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)) {
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(finiteTrialOrgan.cpt)
        || finiteTrialOrgan.cpt < 0.0) return;
    double organSugar = sugarFromCp(finiteTrialOrgan.cpt);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(organSugar) || organSugar < 0.0) return;
    minSugar = Math.min(minSugar, organSugar);
    maxSugar = Math.max(maxSugar, organSugar);
    sugarSum += organSugar;
    finiteOrganCount++;
  }
  if (finiteOrganCount <= 0) {
    minSugar = plantBaseSugar;
    maxSugar = plantBaseSugar;
    sugarSum = plantBaseSugar;
    finiteOrganCount = 1;
  }

  ctx.failedTrialCaptured = true;
  ctx.failedTrialPlantBasePhi = pb.cpt;
  ctx.failedTrialPlantBaseSugar = plantBaseSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMinSugar = minSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMaxSugar = maxSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMeanSugar = sugarSum
      / Double.valueOf(finiteOrganCount).doubleValue();
  ctx.failedTrialMerit = ctx.nonlinearMerit;
}

/** Cached production overload: no graph query during the nonlinear loop. */
static void captureFailedCarbonTransportTrial(PlantBase pb,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx,
        CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  if (pb == null || ctx == null || ctx.converged
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(pb.cpt) || pb.cpt < 0.0
      || !isFiniteCarbonValue(ctx.nonlinearMerit)
      || ctx.nonlinearMerit < 0.0) return;

  double plantBaseSugar = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
  if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(plantBaseSugar) || plantBaseSugar < 0.0) return;

  int finiteOrganCount = 0;
  double minSugar = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  double maxSugar = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;
  double sugarSum = 0.0;
  for (int organIndex = 0;
      organIndex < topology.growingOrgans.size(); organIndex++) {
    GrowingOrgan finiteTrialOrgan = (GrowingOrgan)
        topology.growingOrgans.get(organIndex);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(finiteTrialOrgan.cpt)
        || finiteTrialOrgan.cpt < 0.0) return;
    double organSugar = sugarFromCp(finiteTrialOrgan.cpt);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(organSugar) || organSugar < 0.0) return;
    minSugar = Math.min(minSugar, organSugar);
    maxSugar = Math.max(maxSugar, organSugar);
    sugarSum += organSugar;
    finiteOrganCount++;
  }
  if (finiteOrganCount <= 0) {
    minSugar = plantBaseSugar;
    maxSugar = plantBaseSugar;
    sugarSum = plantBaseSugar;
    finiteOrganCount = 1;
  }

  ctx.failedTrialCaptured = true;
  ctx.failedTrialPlantBasePhi = pb.cpt;
  ctx.failedTrialPlantBaseSugar = plantBaseSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMinSugar = minSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMaxSugar = maxSugar;
  ctx.failedTrialMeanSugar = sugarSum
      / Double.valueOf(finiteOrganCount).doubleValue();
  ctx.failedTrialMerit = ctx.nonlinearMerit;
}

/** Run exactly one nonlinear attempt with the supplied iteration limit. */
static void runCarbonTransportAttempt(PlantBase pb,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx, int iterationLimit,
        CarbonTransportTopology topology) {
  ctx.finalIterationLimit = iterationLimit;
  while (!ctx.converged && ctx.iterationCount < iterationLimit) {
    ctx.iterationCount++;
    long iterationStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    boolean printPerformance = step <= 2 || debug_CT;
    resetCarbonTransportPassState(ctx);
    long phaseStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    linearise(pb, ctx, topology);
    long lineariseMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - phaseStart;
    phaseStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    updateBranchFluxCached(pb, ctx, topology);
    long foldMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - phaseStart;
    phaseStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    updateCarbonPotentialCached(pb, ctx, topology);
    long unfoldMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - phaseStart;
    phaseStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    updateFlowCached(pb, ctx, topology);
    long flowMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - phaseStart;
    captureFailedCarbonTransportTrial(pb, ctx, topology);
    phaseStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
    updateResistenceCached(topology);
    long resistanceMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - phaseStart;
    long iterationMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - iterationStart;
    if (printPerformance) {
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " linearise ms=" + lineariseMillis);
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " fold ms=" + foldMillis);
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " unfold ms=" + unfoldMillis);
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " flow ms=" + flowMillis);
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " resistance ms=" + resistanceMillis);
      println("[CTPERF] iter=" + ctx.iterationCount
          + " total ms=" + iterationMillis);
    }
    if (ctx.iterationCount == 1 && !ctx.retryUsed) {
      touchRunProgress("carbon_iteration_1_complete");
    }
    heartbeatRunProgress();
    if (debug && printFlag) {
      println("error_count " + ctx.iterationCount
          + " Serror " + ctx.convergenceError);
      double sumFlux = sum((* attemptFlux:GrowingOrgan, (
        attemptFlux.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]);
      double sumAbsFlux = sum(Math.abs((* attemptAbsFlux:GrowingOrgan, (
        attemptAbsFlux.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]));
      println("sumFlux " + sumFlux);
      println("RelativeError "
          + ((sumAbsFlux > 0.0) ? sumFlux / sumAbsFlux : 0.0));
    }
    double completedMerit = ctx.nonlinearMerit;
    if (!ctx.converged && ctx.iterationCount < iterationLimit) {
      ctx.dampingFactor = adaptCtDampingFactor(
          ctx.dampingFactor, ctx.previousNonlinearMerit, completedMerit);
    }
    ctx.previousNonlinearMerit = completedMerit;
  }
  ctx.maxIterationReached = !ctx.converged
      && ctx.iterationCount >= iterationLimit;
}

/** Commit a converged hour, or restore without promoting bootstrap state. */
static boolean finalizeCarbonTransportState(PlantBase pb,
        CarbonTransportStateSnapshot snapshot,
        CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  if (ctx.converged) {
    updateCarbonStatus(pb);
    ctx.carbonStatusUpdateCount++;
    ctx.retryConverged = ctx.retryUsed;
    setAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(pb, true);
    return true;
  }
  boolean bootstrapFallback =
      !hasAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(pb);
  restoreCarbonTransportState(pb, snapshot);
  ctx.solverFallbackUsed = true;
  ctx.retryConverged = false;
  ctx.bootstrapFallbackUsed = bootstrapFallback;
  if (bootstrapFallback) {
    updateCarbonStatus(pb);
    ctx.carbonStatusUpdateCount++;
    // Initialization is usable provisionally, but it is not a converged hour.
    setAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(pb, false);
  }
  return false;
}


/**
 * Write compact carbon-transport mass-balance diagnostics for each solved step.
 *
 * <p>Flux columns are diagnostic-only sums of solved organ fluxes: loading is
 * the absolute value of negative source fluxes and unloading is the sum of
 * positive sink fluxes. No explicit storage/boundary term is available here,
 * so netFluxResidual is reported as totalLoading - totalUnloading.</p>
 */
static void writeCtMassBalanceDiagnostics(
        PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) {
  long organCount = count((* gCount:GrowingOrgan, (
    gCount.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *));
  double minCp = 0.0;
  double maxCp = 0.0;
  double meanCp = 0.0;
  double minSugar = 0.0;
  double maxSugar = 0.0;
  double meanSugar = 0.0;
  if (organCount > 0) {
    minCp = min((* gMin:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMin.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    maxCp = max((* gMax:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMax.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    meanCp = mean((* gMean:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMean.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    minSugar = sugarFromCp(minCp);
    maxSugar = sugarFromCp(maxCp);
    // Diagnostic mean sugar is computed from mean Phi to keep this source-only patch
    // compatible with older RGG aggregate-expression parsing.
    meanSugar = sugarFromCp(meanCp);
  }

  CarbonTransportMassBalanceDiagnosticOutputData row =
      new CarbonTransportMassBalanceDiagnosticOutputData();
  row.timestamp = timestamp;
  row.step = step;
  row.year = year;
  row.dayOfYear = dayOfYear;
  row.hourOfDay = hourOfDay;
  row.scenario = scenario;
  row.simuuid = simUUID;
  row.plantNumber = pb.plantNumber;
  row.fieldInstanceId = pb.fieldInstanceId;
  row.day = day;
  row.hour = hourOfDay;
  row.useCPStyleCTResponse = true;
  row.iterationCount = ctx.iterationCount;
  row.convergenceError = ctx.convergenceError;
  row.totalLoading = ctx.totalLoading;
  row.totalUnloading = ctx.totalUnloading;
  row.netFluxResidual = ctx.netFluxResidual;
  row.relativeFluxResidual = ctx.relativeNetFluxResidual;
  row.minCp = minCp;
  row.maxCp = maxCp;
  row.meanCp = meanCp;
  row.minSugar = minSugar;
  row.maxSugar = maxSugar;
  row.meanSugar = meanSugar;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount;
  row.ctPlantBaseResidual = pb.ctPlantBaseResidual;
  row.ctPlantBaseDenominator = pb.ctPlantBaseDenominator;
  row.absoluteFluxError = ctx.convergenceError;
  row.relativeFluxConvergenceError = ctx.relativeFluxError;
  row.ctPlantBaseAbsoluteResidual = ctx.plantBaseResidual;
  row.ctPlantBaseRelativeResidual = ctx.plantBaseRelativeResidual;
  row.ctDampingFactor = ctx.dampingFactor;
  row.ctRawPlantBasePhi = ctx.rawPlantBasePhi;
  row.ctAcceptedPlantBasePhi = ctx.acceptedPlantBasePhi;
  row.ctConverged = ctx.converged;
  row.ctMaxIterationReached = ctx.maxIterationReached;
  row.ctNonlinearMerit = ctx.nonlinearMerit;
  row.ctRetryUsed = ctx.retryUsed;
  row.ctRetryConverged = ctx.retryConverged;
  row.ctSolverFallbackUsed = ctx.solverFallbackUsed;
  row.ctInvalidUnfoldTrialCount = ctx.totalInvalidUnfoldTrialCount;
  row.ctFinalIterationLimit = ctx.finalIterationLimit;
  row.ctBootstrapFallbackUsed = ctx.bootstrapFallbackUsed;
  row.ctHasAcceptedHourlyState =
      hasAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(pb);
  row.ctStoredPlantBaseSugar = pb.sugarConcentration_phloem;
  row.ctPlantBaseSugarFromPhi = isValidPhi(pb.cpt)
      ? sugarFromCp(pb.cpt) : 0.0;
  row.ctAcceptedHourlyPlantBaseSugar = row.ctHasAcceptedHourlyState
      ? row.ctPlantBaseSugarFromPhi : 0.0;
  row.ctFailedTrialPlantBasePhi = ctx.failedTrialPlantBasePhi;
  row.ctFailedTrialPlantBaseSugar = ctx.failedTrialPlantBaseSugar;
  row.ctFailedTrialMinSugar = ctx.failedTrialMinSugar;
  row.ctFailedTrialMaxSugar = ctx.failedTrialMaxSugar;
  row.ctFailedTrialMeanSugar = ctx.failedTrialMeanSugar;
  row.ctFailedTrialMerit = ctx.failedTrialMerit;
  row.sumLocalJ = ctx.sumLocalJ;
  row.pbFoldedJ = ctx.pbFoldedJ;
  row.closureResidual = ctx.closureResidual;
  row.closureScale = ctx.closureScale;
  row.relativeClosureResidual = ctx.relativeClosureResidual;
  row.closureNormalizedError = ctx.closureNormalizedError;
  row.netFluxIdentityResidual = ctx.netFluxIdentityResidual;
  row.totalGrowingOrganCount = ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount;
  row.foldedGrowingOrganCount = ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount;
  row.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount = ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount;
  row.foldCoverageComplete = ctx.foldCoverageComplete;
  row.unfoldCoverageComplete = ctx.unfoldCoverageComplete;
  row.sumLeafJ = ctx.sumLeafStoredJ;
  row.sumLeafTaylorJ = ctx.sumLeafTaylorJ;
  row.sumPetioleJ = ctx.sumPetioleStoredJ;
  row.sumPetioleTaylorJ = ctx.sumPetioleTaylorJ;
  row.sumShootJ = ctx.sumShootStoredJ;
  row.sumShootTaylorJ = ctx.sumShootTaylorJ;
  row.sumFruitJ = ctx.sumFruitStoredJ;
  row.sumFruitTaylorJ = ctx.sumFruitTaylorJ;
  row.sumFlowerJ = ctx.sumFlowerStoredJ;
  row.sumFlowerTaylorJ = ctx.sumFlowerTaylorJ;
  row.sumFineRootJ = ctx.sumFineRootStoredJ;
  row.sumFineRootTaylorJ = ctx.sumFineRootTaylorJ;
  row.sumStructuralRootJ = ctx.sumStructuralRootStoredJ;
  row.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ = ctx.sumStructuralRootTaylorJ;
  row.sumFruitExactUnloading = ctx.sumFruitExactUnloading;
  row.sumFruitExactActive = ctx.sumFruitExactActive;
  row.sumFruitExactMassFlow = ctx.sumFruitExactMassFlow;
  row.sumFruitStoredUnloading = ctx.sumFruitStoredUnloading;
  row.fruitLinearizationResidual = ctx.fruitLinearizationResidual;
  row.fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual =
      ctx.fruitLinearizationRelativeResidual;
  row.maxFruitLinearizationResidual =
      ctx.maxFruitLinearizationResidual;
  row.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual =
      ctx.maxFruitLinearizationRelativeResidual;
  row.maxFruitResidualOrganID = ctx.maxFruitResidualOrganID;
  row.fruitStoredVsExactResidual = ctx.fruitStoredVsExactResidual;
  row.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual = ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointResidual;
  row.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual =
      ctx.maxFruitTaylorPointRelativeResidual;
  row.simpleRootActive = ctx.simpleRootActive;
  row.simpleRootTopologyValid = ctx.simpleRootTopologyValid;
  row.simpleRootFoldValid = ctx.simpleRootFoldValid;
  row.simpleRootUnfoldValid = ctx.simpleRootUnfoldValid;
  row.simpleRootDoubleFoldCount = ctx.simpleRootDoubleFoldCount;
  row.simpleRootMinLayer = ctx.simpleRootMinLayer;
  row.simpleRootMaxLayer = ctx.simpleRootMaxLayer;
  row.simpleRootLayerCount = ctx.simpleRootLayerCount;
  row.simpleStructuralRootExpected = ctx.simpleStructuralRootExpected;
  row.simpleStructuralRootFolded = ctx.simpleStructuralRootFolded;
  row.simpleStructuralRootUnfolded = ctx.simpleStructuralRootUnfolded;
  row.simpleFineRootExpected = ctx.simpleFineRootExpected;
  row.simpleFineRootFolded = ctx.simpleFineRootFolded;
  row.simpleFineRootUnfolded = ctx.simpleFineRootUnfolded;
  row.simpleRootLocalJ = ctx.simpleRootLocalJ;
  row.simpleRootFoldedJ = ctx.simpleRootFoldedJ;
  row.simpleRootClosureResidual = ctx.simpleRootClosureResidual;
  row.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual =
      ctx.simpleRootRelativeClosureResidual;
  DiagnosticTableCoordinator.writeCarbonTransportMassBalance(row);
}

/**
 * Execute one full carbon-transport solve for the current time step.
 *
 * <p><b>Sequence</b>
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@link #linearise(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — per-organ (a,b)</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateBranchFlux(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — fold to branch (a,b)</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — unfold cp across the plant graph</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateFlow(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — update j and residuals</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateResistence(PlantBase)} — refresh transport coefficients</li>
 *   <li>Repeat steps 1–5 until mixed flux-change and PlantBase boundary
 *       criteria pass, or exactly {@code CT_MAX_ITERATIONS} passes are used.</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase)} — final per-organ status & Mcf.</li>
 * </ol></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Convergence control</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>The flux criterion combines absolute and graph-scale relative error.</li>
 *   <li>The PlantBase boundary residual must also pass its mixed criterion, so
 *       small damping cannot create false convergence.</li>
 *   <li>Whole-plant closure and fold/unfold coverage remain diagnostic-only in
 *       this isolation patch. Invalid simple-root topology or incomplete
 *       simple-root fold/unfold coverage still invalidates the solve.</li>
 *   <li>Fruit solved-current versus pure exact-unloading residuals are emitted
 *       separately for diagnosis and are not an additional convergence gate.</li>
 *   <li>Adaptive damping is based on the previous complete nonlinear pass.</li>
	 *   <li>The normal solve starts with the configured initial damping. A failed
	 *       30-pass solve is retried once with alpha 0.1 and a 60-pass limit. A
	 *       complete finite normal trial warm-starts that retry; invalid trials first
	 *       roll back to the pre-attempt state.</li>
 *   <li>If the first retry also fails, the initialized state is restored and
 *       used once as a non-converged bootstrap without marking it accepted.</li>
 *   <li>After one converged hourly state exists, a failed retry restores that
 *       accepted pre-hour state without committing the failed iterate.</li>
	 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Scope</b> — Only organs matching the supplied plant identity are read or updated.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */

static void updateC_Transport(PlantBase pb)
{
		if (pb == null) {
			throw new IllegalArgumentException("Carbon transport requires a PlantBase instance.");
		}
		long solveStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
		boolean printPerformance = step <= 2 || debug_CT;
		touchRunProgress("carbon_start", "started");
		if (printPerformance) println("[CTPERF] step=" + step + " start");
		long topologyStart = System.currentTimeMillis();
		GrowingOrgan[] collectedOrgans = array((* ctTopologyOrgan:GrowingOrgan, (
			ctTopologyOrgan.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
		) *));
		CarbonTransportTopology topology = buildCarbonTransportTopology(
			pb, collectedOrgans);
		long topologyMillis = System.currentTimeMillis() - topologyStart;
		if (printPerformance) {
			println("[CTPERF] topology/owner-resolution ms=" + topologyMillis);
			println("[CTPERF] growingOrgans=" + topology.growingOrgans.size()
				+ " internodes=" + topology.internodesById.size()
				+ " petioles=" + topology.petiolesById.size()
				+ " leaves=" + topology.leavesById.size()
				+ " fruits=" + topology.fruitsById.size()
				+ " flowers=" + topology.flowersById.size()
				+ " structuralRoots=" + topology.structuralRoots.size()
				+ " fineRoots=" + topology.fineRoots.size());
			println("[CTPERF] owners ambiguousLeaves="
				+ topology.ambiguousLeafOwners + " missingLeaves="
				+ topology.missingLeafOwners + " ambiguousFineRoots="
				+ topology.ambiguousFineRootOwners + " missingFineRoots="
				+ topology.missingFineRootOwners);
		}
		if (!topology.valid) {
			touchRunProgress("carbon_topology_complete", "failed");
			throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid carbon-transport topology: "
				+ topology.error + " ambiguousLeafOwners="
				+ topology.ambiguousLeafOwners + " missingLeafOwners="
				+ topology.missingLeafOwners + " ambiguousFineRootOwners="
				+ topology.ambiguousFineRootOwners + " missingFineRootOwners="
				+ topology.missingFineRootOwners);
		}
		touchRunProgress("carbon_topology_complete");
		boolean hadAcceptedHourlyState =
			hasAcceptedHourlyCarbonTransportState(pb);
		if (!hadAcceptedHourlyState) {
			prepareInitialCarbonTransportSnapshotState(pb);
		}
		CarbonTransportStateSnapshot acceptedState =
			snapshotCarbonTransportState(pb, topology);
		CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx = new CarbonTransportSolveContext();
		ctx.dampingFactor = CT_DAMPING_INITIAL;
		ctx.finalIterationLimit = CT_MAX_ITERATIONS;

		// Each pass is one complete re-linearise/fold/unfold/reconstruct cycle.
		runCarbonTransportAttempt(pb, ctx, CT_MAX_ITERATIONS, topology);
		if (shouldStartCarbonTransportRetry(ctx)) {
			if (!shouldWarmStartCarbonTransportRetry(ctx)) {
				restoreCarbonTransportState(pb, acceptedState);
			}
			CarbonTransportSolveContext retryContext =
				createCarbonTransportRetryContext(ctx);
			runCarbonTransportAttempt(
				pb, retryContext, CT_RETRY_MAX_ITERATIONS, topology);
			ctx = retryContext;
		}

		updateFinalFruitCarbonDiagnostics(ctx, topology);
		boolean accepted = finalizeCarbonTransportState(
			pb, acceptedState, ctx);
		if (!accepted) {
			if (!hadAcceptedHourlyState) {
				println("WARN(CT): first solve failed; using initialized transport state for bootstrap");
			} else {
				println("WARN(CT): normal solve and single retry failed for plant "
					+ pb.plantNumber + "; restored accepted pre-hour transport state");
			}
		}
		if(outputCarbonTransportDiagnostics) {
			writeCtMassBalanceDiagnostics(pb, ctx);
		}
		touchRunProgress("carbon_solve_complete",
			accepted ? "accepted" : "fallback");
		if (printPerformance) {
			println("[CTPERF] coverage folded="
				+ ctx.foldedGrowingOrganCount + "/"
				+ ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount + " unfolded="
				+ ctx.unfoldedGrowingOrganCount + "/"
				+ ctx.totalGrowingOrganCount);
			println("[CTPERF] solve total ms="
				+ (System.currentTimeMillis() - solveStart));
		}


	}




/**
 * Utilities for coupling xylem pull with phloem transport in the linearised
 * carbon-potential (Φ) framework.
 *
 * <h3>Conventions</h3>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Local linearisation: {@code j ≈ a + b·Φ} at the distal (downstream) end of a segment.</li>
 *   <li>Potential drop across one segment: {@code Φ_top = Φ_bot − r·j − x_p}.</li>
 *   <li><b>This class stores</b> {@code x_p ≥ 0} as an extra drop (magnitude only).</li>
 *   <li>If you instead store Alla’s signed pull {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0}, use the notes under each method.</li>
 * </ul>
 */
  /**
   * Exact <b>UNFOLD</b>: compute the top potential {@code cpt} from the bottom potential {@code cpb}
   * through one transport segment with resistance {@code r}, distal linearisation {@code (a,b)},
   * and xylem pull magnitude {@code x_p ≥ 0}.
   *
   * <p><b>Governing relations</b></p>
   * <pre>
   * j = a + b·cpt
   * cpt = cpb − r·j − x_p
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Derivation</b></p>
   * Substitute the first into the second:
   * <pre>
   * cpt = cpb − r·(a + b·cpt) − x_p
   * (1 + b·r)·cpt = cpb − a·r − x_p
   * </pre>
   * Hence the exact unfold:
   * <pre>
   * cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p) / (1 + b·r)
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Alla’s convention (optional)</b> — if you store {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0} (signed pull),
   * pass {@code x_p = -x_p^{(−)}} here, or use the equivalent form
   * {@code cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p^{(−)})/(1 + b·r)}.</p>
   *
   * @param cpb bottom carbon potential Φ (segment inlet)
   * @param a   distal intercept of j–Φ linearisation (units of flux)
   * @param b   distal slope of j–Φ linearisation (per-Φ)
   * @param r   segment phloem resistance (Φ per unit flux)
   * @param xp  xylem-pull magnitude (extra drop) {@code x_p ≥ 0}
   * @return    top carbon potential Φ: {@code cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p)/(1 + b·r)}
   */
   //not sure why but actually the first order expansion works better than the exact form
   //maybe due to the whole method is using linear operation
  public static double unfoldPhi(double cpb, double a, double b, double r, double xp) {
    return (cpb - a * r - xp) / (1.0 + b * r);
  }

  /**
   * Exact <b>FOLD</b>: map distal linear coefficients {@code (a,b)} through one segment
   * to an upstream view {@code (a', b')} such that {@code j = a' + b'·cpb}.
   *
   * <p><b>Derivation</b></p>
   * Start with {@code j = a + b·cpt} and plug the exact unfold:
   * <pre>
   * j = a + b·(cpb − a·r − x_p)/(1 + b·r)
   *   = [a + b·cpb − b·x_p] / (1 + b·r)
   *   = a' + b'·cpb
   * </pre>
   * Therefore,
   * <pre>
   * a' = (a − b·x_p) / (1 + b·r)
   * b' =  b         / (1 + b·r)
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Sanity check</b> — With these {@code a', b'} and the unfold above,
   * {@code a + b·cpt ≡ a' + b'·cpb} (identity), which preserves mass balance and improves stability.</p>
   *
   * <p><b>Alla’s convention (optional)</b> — if you store {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0}, use
   * {@code a' = (a + b·x_p^{(−)})/(1 + b·r)} (the “plus” seen in her code), with the same {@code b'}.</p>
   *
   * @param a  distal intercept
   * @param b  distal slope
   * @param r  segment resistance
   * @param xp xylem-pull magnitude (extra drop) {@code x_p ≥ 0}
   * @return   a 2-element array {@code [a', b']} (upstream coefficients)
   */
  public static double[] foldCoeffs(double a, double b, double r, double xp) {
    double denom = 1.0 + b * r;
    double aPrime = (a - b * xp) / denom;
    double bPrime =  b / denom;
    return new double[] { aPrime, bPrime };
  }
